WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:50.445 --> 00:00:53.112
<i>Last night,
I dreamt I went to Manderley again.</i>


00:00:53.904 --> 00:00:58.195
<i>I dreamt that where our drive once lay,
a dark and tortured jungle grew.</i>


00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:04.528
<i>Nature had come into her own
and yet the house still stood.</i>


00:01:05.362 --> 00:01:06.362
<i>Manderley.</i>


00:01:06.987 --> 00:01:09.612
<i>Secretive and silent
as it had always been.</i>


00:01:10.237 --> 00:01:12.154
<i>Risen from the dead.</i>


00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:19.529
<i>Like all dreamers, I was allowed
to pass through my memory.</i>


00:01:20.195 --> 00:01:21.904
<i>Spanning the years like a bridge.</i>


00:01:24.195 --> 00:01:29.903
<i>Back to that summer in Monte Carlo
when I knew nothing and had no prospects.</i>


00:01:44.529 --> 00:01:45.404
Did you say eight?


00:01:45.487 --> 00:01:46.904
<i>- Huit.
- Yes.</i>


00:01:49.695 --> 00:01:51.404
<i>- Merci. Au revoir.
- Au revoir.</i>


00:01:58.194 --> 00:02:00.819
<i>I can see
the girl I was so clearly,</i>


00:02:00.903 --> 00:02:03.194
<i>even if I no longer recognize her.</i>


00:02:06.904 --> 00:02:09.945
<i>And I wonder what my life
would have been without Mrs. Van Hopper.</i>


00:02:11.945 --> 00:02:13.279
<i>Without that job.</i>


00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.194
<i>Funny to think
that the course of my existence</i>


00:02:16.278 --> 00:02:18.611
<i>hung like a thread upon her curiosity.</i>


00:02:20.028 --> 00:02:22.944
<i>If it wasn't for her,
I would never have gone to Manderley...</i>


00:02:24.111 --> 00:02:25.778
<i>and would never have met you.</i>


00:02:26.861 --> 00:02:27.944
Mrs. Van Hopper.


00:02:28.861 --> 00:02:30.361
What kept you?


00:02:30.444 --> 00:02:34.112
I'm sorry. I had to wait
for a package at the post office. I...


00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:35.850
I believe it's from your nephew.


00:02:35.904 --> 00:02:39.737
Oh, photographs of his honeymoon
with that ghastly girl, I imagine.


00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:40.819
Open it.


00:02:41.236 --> 00:02:44.903
- Get a table downstairs for lunch.
- Yes. One o'clock as usual?


00:02:44.986 --> 00:02:48.486
- Now. I've just seen Maxim de Winter.
- Oh, right.


00:02:48.569 --> 00:02:50.278
Still heartbroken, by the look of it.


00:02:50.361 --> 00:02:51.944
He's a friend of yours?


00:02:52.528 --> 00:02:55.278
Maxim de Winter, owner of Manderley.


00:02:55.944 --> 00:02:58.403
- One of the finest homes in England.
- Oh, yes.


00:02:58.486 --> 00:03:01.111
His wife died last year.
He's in dire need of company.


00:03:01.694 --> 00:03:04.904
<i>- Have the maître d' seat him next to me.
- Oh.</i>


00:03:09.944 --> 00:03:11.153
You'll have to tip.


00:03:14.944 --> 00:03:17.111
Honestly, with everything
I'm teaching you,


00:03:17.194 --> 00:03:18.234
you ought to be paying me.


00:03:19.111 --> 00:03:21.153
- Thank you, Mrs. Van Hopper.
- Stupid girl.


00:03:29.153 --> 00:03:30.693
<i>- Bonjour.
- Mademoiselle.</i>


00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:33.153
Ah! Madam Van Hopper's usual table?


00:03:33.236 --> 00:03:34.694
<i>Oh, yes, thank you. Merci.</i>


00:03:34.778 --> 00:03:36.028
Oh, no. Um...


00:03:36.111 --> 00:03:40.028
Wait, sorry. She was wondering
if a Mr. de Winter could sit with her.


00:03:40.111 --> 00:03:42.153
<i>- Monsieur Maxim de Winter?
- Oui.</i>


00:03:42.778 --> 00:03:45.694
It is the choice of Mr. de Winter
where he wishes to be seated.


00:03:45.778 --> 00:03:47.236
Oh, yes, of course.


00:03:47.903 --> 00:03:48.903
<i>Merci.</i>


00:03:50.319 --> 00:03:53.653
So sorry. Is that not enough?
Um, here. I've got more.


00:03:53.736 --> 00:03:55.235
Oh!


00:03:55.318 --> 00:03:57.277
<i>God, I'm so sorry, monsieur.</i>


00:03:58.152 --> 00:03:59.610
Just one moment.


00:03:59.693 --> 00:04:01.903
Don't do it.
I've heard he's a terrible bore.


00:04:02.486 --> 00:04:05.236
- Excuse me?
- This de Winter chap.


00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:06.319
Thank you.


00:04:08.111 --> 00:04:10.694
<i>Monsieur de Winter,
please, this way.</i>


00:04:24.818 --> 00:04:26.943
<i>Des huîtres, une douzaine.</i>


00:04:27.027 --> 00:04:28.277
<i>"Des huîtres, une douzaine."</i>


00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:34.319
Maxim de Winter. Well, I never.
I had no idea you were in Monte.


00:04:34.403 --> 00:04:36.153
You must join us.


00:04:36.236 --> 00:04:40.486
Edie Van Hopper.
I think you remember my nephew. Billy?


00:04:40.569 --> 00:04:44.110
You met him at Blenheim last fall.
Billy Whitney. He's about my height.


00:04:44.193 --> 00:04:47.652
He's got sandy hair
and he's got a bit of a lazy eye.


00:04:47.735 --> 00:04:50.693
I can't imagine how I could've forgotten.
Do give my regards to Billy.


00:04:50.777 --> 00:04:51.902
Oh, would you know?


00:04:51.985 --> 00:04:55.318
He's married,
and to the most enchanting girl.


00:04:55.402 --> 00:04:56.586
- Is he?
- He sent photographs.


00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:59.236
I'll show you. Come here.
The wedding was divine.


00:04:59.319 --> 00:05:01.403
I believe you,
but I prefer to lunch alone.


00:05:02.736 --> 00:05:04.736
- Good day, Miss Van Hopper.
- Oh, no.


00:05:04.819 --> 00:05:08.360
What? We're not related. She's staff.


00:05:11.485 --> 00:05:14.402
Well, I mean,
I guess you could call her my ward.


00:05:14.485 --> 00:05:17.610
Hmm, I see. Now, if you'll excuse me.


00:05:17.693 --> 00:05:20.943
Darling, fetch those photographs.
Mr. de Winter would love to see them.


00:05:21.027 --> 00:05:22.985
No, please. Don't trouble yourself.


00:05:23.068 --> 00:05:25.443
- It's unnecessary.
- No trouble at all!


00:05:25.527 --> 00:05:29.569
Not at all. Go along. Quickly.
No, no. She'll be down in a jiffy.


00:05:43.027 --> 00:05:44.735
This is my favorite part.


00:05:44.818 --> 00:05:46.860
I asked her to get the photographs,


00:05:46.943 --> 00:05:50.902
and she darts from the table,
and then she's gone. Doesn't come back.


00:05:50.985 --> 00:05:53.527
I thought, "Oh, God, don't tell me
she started sketching."


00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:55.902
Oh, no, she's an artist.


00:05:56.651 --> 00:06:01.693
Anyway, she comes running back down,
reeking of cheap rose water.


00:06:04.902 --> 00:06:06.443
<i>I mean, the smell of it!</i>


00:06:07.485 --> 00:06:10.527
Show me an eligible bachelor


00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:16.568
and I will show you a room full of women
acting like they've lost their minds.


00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:19.277
It's too late.


00:06:19.735 --> 00:06:21.067
- Sorry.
- Never mind, sit down.


00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:24.317
Related. I mean, imagine.


00:06:24.401 --> 00:06:28.318
I loved the Manderley ball.
It was just so glamorous.


00:06:28.402 --> 00:06:30.527
I suppose
that's all stopped since the tragedy.


00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:33.277
Such a shocking thing that happened.


00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.068
- How do you explain it?
- Awful.


00:06:35.152 --> 00:06:37.068
- He adored her!
- Mmm.


00:06:37.152 --> 00:06:38.277
His Rebecca.


00:06:45.027 --> 00:06:46.692
Morning, Mrs. Van Hopper.


00:06:51.442 --> 00:06:53.817
Mrs. Van Hopper?


00:06:53.901 --> 00:06:54.984
Are you all right?


00:06:55.067 --> 00:06:57.568
I'm sick.
I'm sick.


00:06:57.652 --> 00:07:02.235
I'm... I was sick all night.


00:07:02.318 --> 00:07:05.152
<i>- Call the... call the medecin.
- Okay.</i>


00:07:06.527 --> 00:07:09.693
- Call them right now. The doctor.
- All right.


00:07:10.984 --> 00:07:13.359
Where is the bucket? Where's the bucket?


00:07:13.442 --> 00:07:15.901
I'll get the bucket! Here, I've got it.


00:07:19.192 --> 00:07:20.817
<i>You are waiting for madame?</i>


00:07:20.901 --> 00:07:23.859
Oh, no. She's unwell.
The doctor told her to rest.


00:07:23.942 --> 00:07:25.318
So, it's just me today.


00:07:25.402 --> 00:07:28.777
It is not possible.
The terrace is for guests only.


00:07:29.777 --> 00:07:33.360
But I'm a lady's companion... really?


00:07:33.443 --> 00:07:35.151
Yes, it is not for staff.


00:07:38.817 --> 00:07:42.567
<i>Monsieur? The young lady will be
joining me. Set another place, please.</i>


00:07:42.651 --> 00:07:44.291
<i>Bien sûr, Monsieur de Winter.</i>


00:07:44.317 --> 00:07:46.077
No, please.
I couldn't possibly.


00:07:46.151 --> 00:07:47.526
It's absolutely fine.


00:07:47.609 --> 00:07:50.234
- We needn't talk unless we feel like it.
- Oh.


00:07:51.401 --> 00:07:54.485
You... you didn't have to do that.


00:07:54.568 --> 00:07:56.735
My motives were entirely selfish.


00:07:56.818 --> 00:07:59.651
This is yesterday's paper.
I've already read it.


00:08:01.317 --> 00:08:02.692
Thank you. It's very kind.


00:08:06.026 --> 00:08:09.442
- So, what is it you do for...
- I'm what's called "a lady's companion."


00:08:10.026 --> 00:08:12.984
If a lady has to pay for company,
that says something about the lady.


00:08:15.151 --> 00:08:16.511
May I take your order?


00:08:17.526 --> 00:08:19.776
<i>Des huîtres, une douzaine.</i>


00:08:19.859 --> 00:08:21.234
For breakfast?


00:08:21.317 --> 00:08:23.651
<i>You heard her. Et encore du café.</i>


00:08:23.734 --> 00:08:26.109
<i>Bien, Monsieur de Winter. Mademoiselle.</i>


00:08:28.317 --> 00:08:31.567
If it's not rude, why her?


00:08:32.276 --> 00:08:35.151
You would make an excellent
companion for any number of people.


00:08:35.234 --> 00:08:38.609
I've always wanted to travel,
so there's that, and £90 a year.


00:08:41.109 --> 00:08:44.151
I know that's not very much to you,
but it's a lot to me.


00:08:45.276 --> 00:08:47.484
I suppose you can
set a price on loneliness.


00:08:47.567 --> 00:08:50.566
It's odd, isn't it?
Some people seem perfectly happy alone


00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:54.109
while others just need someone
to pass the time with. Doesn't matter who.


00:08:55.192 --> 00:08:56.192
Which are you?


00:08:56.234 --> 00:09:01.109
Well, my parents are dead, so...
I'm used to being alone.


00:09:03.359 --> 00:09:04.192
Ah.


00:09:04.276 --> 00:09:05.316
Here comes your breakfast.


00:09:07.651 --> 00:09:09.817
<i>Et voilà. Une douzaine d'huîtres.</i>


00:09:11.942 --> 00:09:13.981
I've always wanted to try them, so...


00:09:14.691 --> 00:09:15.983
Try them before they get warm.


00:09:32.692 --> 00:09:35.692
Thank you so much.
I've never spoken so much in my life.


00:09:35.776 --> 00:09:37.251
It was very impressive.


00:09:37.275 --> 00:09:40.733
- And I'm sorry about the oysters, too. I...
- No, that was fine.


00:09:41.358 --> 00:09:42.816
Thank you very much. I...


00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:45.733
I haven't enjoyed myself
like that for quite a long time.


00:09:49.858 --> 00:09:50.901
<i>À bientôt.</i>


00:10:11.816 --> 00:10:12.816
Hello?


00:10:17.525 --> 00:10:19.984
<i>- A note from the front desk.
- Merci. Madame's indisposed.</i>


00:10:20.067 --> 00:10:22.107
<i>- I'll take it to her.
- It's for you, mademoiselle.</i>


00:10:23.817 --> 00:10:24.817
<i>Merci.</i>


00:10:27.358 --> 00:10:29.650
What do they want?


00:10:31.275 --> 00:10:32.275
Um...


00:10:33.108 --> 00:10:35.150
It was just the front desk, they were...


00:10:36.941 --> 00:10:38.191
<i>wondering how you are.</i>


00:10:57.066 --> 00:10:58.483
So how did you escape?


00:10:58.566 --> 00:11:01.733
I said I had a tennis lesson.
She's been on at me to improve my game.


00:11:01.816 --> 00:11:02.816
Sneaky.


00:11:05.525 --> 00:11:08.066
- So where do you want to go?
- Anywhere is fine.


00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:10.316
There must be
somewhere you want to see.


00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.941
Well, it's quite far.


00:11:12.483 --> 00:11:14.566
Good. I could use the fresh air.


00:11:15.232 --> 00:11:17.065
Is this
a 3.5-liter Bentley?


00:11:17.149 --> 00:11:19.400
It is.
How do you know so much about cars?


00:11:19.483 --> 00:11:22.566
Oh, my father,
he loved them.


00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:25.733
If I may ask,
when did your parents pass away?


00:11:27.275 --> 00:11:29.025
Two winters ago. Influenza.


00:11:29.108 --> 00:11:31.233
Well, my mother
died of influenza, and my...


00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:34.191
father died just four days later.


00:11:36.733 --> 00:11:38.983
Do you think a person
could die of a broken heart?


00:11:43.190 --> 00:11:46.482
- That was thoughtless of me. I'm sorry.
- No.


00:11:52.525 --> 00:11:54.483
It's all right.


00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:56.941
All part of the plan.


00:11:59.733 --> 00:12:01.816
EXOTIC GARDEN
PLEASE DO NOT TOUCH ANYTHING


00:12:07.982 --> 00:12:10.274
<i>There's a cactus,
it's native to Mexico,</i>


00:12:10.357 --> 00:12:13.107
<i>and it grows to 65 feet tall.</i>


00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:16.983
It lives for 200 years,
but it doesn't flower until it's 70.


00:12:17.066 --> 00:12:19.400
Where do you learn this stuff?


00:12:19.483 --> 00:12:22.108
I read about it.
Everything I know is from books.


00:12:22.191 --> 00:12:27.566
I haven't really experienced anything yet.
I plan to before I'm old.


00:12:35.857 --> 00:12:36.857
Look!


00:12:52.150 --> 00:12:53.524
Have you been here before?


00:12:55.649 --> 00:12:59.357
Years ago. On my honeymoon.


00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:11.815
- How did your wife...
- Please... let's not.


00:13:42.439 --> 00:13:43.814
Mr. de Winter.


00:13:48.024 --> 00:13:49.649
- Go on.
- Oh, no. I couldn't.


00:13:49.732 --> 00:13:52.524
Yes. Yes, you can.
You know how, don't you?


00:13:52.607 --> 00:13:55.149
Um, well, yes, I...


00:13:55.232 --> 00:13:57.690
Well, good.
As long as you didn't learn from a book.


00:14:03.649 --> 00:14:06.939
Will you tell me about Manderley?
I hear it's beautiful.


00:14:07.023 --> 00:14:11.939
It is. Yeah. Manderley,
it's more than a house. It's my life.


00:14:12.523 --> 00:14:16.065
It's been passed from father to son
and father to son for centuries.


00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:18.065
Until now, anyway.


00:14:19.482 --> 00:14:23.524
You see, if I die without an heir,
it goes to my sister.


00:14:23.607 --> 00:14:27.440
And her sons are nice boys,
but they're just not de Winters.


00:14:39.773 --> 00:14:40.648
There we go.


00:14:40.731 --> 00:14:43.357
Well, thank you
for getting us home safely.


00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.024
Don't forget your things.


00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:47.524
Sir, give us a hand?


00:14:49.857 --> 00:14:51.315
This is what I need from you.


00:14:51.399 --> 00:14:54.399
Would you grab that bag
and just lift at the same time?


00:14:55.065 --> 00:14:56.606
One, two, three.


00:15:00.481 --> 00:15:01.939
Put that back, please.


00:15:02.023 --> 00:15:03.898
Yes, of course. I'm sorry. I...


00:15:04.606 --> 00:15:06.898
Leave the keys with the valet. Good night.


00:15:07.773 --> 00:15:08.856
Good night.


00:15:20.273 --> 00:15:21.564
Hello.


00:15:24.523 --> 00:15:26.773
The nurse left an hour ago.


00:15:27.606 --> 00:15:31.398
The tennis coach only had
a late session free...


00:15:32.773 --> 00:15:34.939
and I was practicing my serve.


00:15:37.189 --> 00:15:39.564
A tennis lesson in the dark?


00:15:41.565 --> 00:15:42.565
Yes.


00:15:50.189 --> 00:15:52.981
Rebecca from Max.
Max from Rebecca.


00:15:53.064 --> 00:15:56.981
You stupid girl.
Why would I look at his personal book?


00:16:18.648 --> 00:16:20.773
<i>For you. From Monsieur de Winter.</i>


00:16:36.105 --> 00:16:39.022
<i>Pour moi? Merci.</i>


00:16:45.064 --> 00:16:47.148
- I'm off.
- What have you got on?


00:16:47.231 --> 00:16:48.814
I can see right through it.


00:16:48.898 --> 00:16:49.773
Oh.


00:16:49.856 --> 00:16:52.689
- You wearing any undergarments?
- Yes, of course.


00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:03.397
I'm trying to paint beautiful houses.


00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:07.855
Actually, you don't need
your tennis racket. All right.


00:17:09.273 --> 00:17:10.523
<i>Mademoiselle.</i>


00:17:11.773 --> 00:17:12.773
<i>Merci.</i>


00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:28.022
<i>- What are you doing?
- Oh, you'll see.</i>


00:17:35.563 --> 00:17:39.981
Imagine if you could
bottle a memory like scent.


00:17:42.648 --> 00:17:45.106
Then, whenever you wanted,
you could open it.


00:17:46.273 --> 00:17:48.730
It'd be like
living the moment all over again.


00:17:51.147 --> 00:17:54.855
And what particular moments
in your young life would you bottle?


00:17:56.022 --> 00:17:58.605
This week. Now. Every minute of it.


00:18:00.772 --> 00:18:01.980
Never forget it.


00:18:04.813 --> 00:18:08.314
And any memories you didn't want,
you could simply throw away.


00:18:12.813 --> 00:18:14.230
"Come for a drive."


00:18:14.313 --> 00:18:15.522
"Lunch at the Cap."


00:18:17.313 --> 00:18:18.397
The beach.


00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:34.522
But I love the coast down here.


00:18:36.022 --> 00:18:37.147
It's so beautiful.


00:18:38.938 --> 00:18:40.188
Oh, there we go!


00:18:40.272 --> 00:18:41.730
What are you looking at?


00:18:41.813 --> 00:18:45.022
- Um, well, it's...
- Let me see.


00:18:45.605 --> 00:18:46.897
I wouldn't if I were you.


00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:49.230
No...
Well, it's just as well you're not...


00:18:55.938 --> 00:18:58.147
- Sorry.
- That's all right.


00:18:59.605 --> 00:19:01.562
Come on.
Let's go for a swim.


00:19:02.812 --> 00:19:05.105
Come on. Come on!


00:19:05.938 --> 00:19:08.397
- Come in!
- No!


00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:10.813
- Why not?
- I don't want to!


00:19:10.897 --> 00:19:12.457
What are you afraid of?


00:19:12.522 --> 00:19:15.730
It's too cold. No, it's freezing.


00:19:15.813 --> 00:19:17.563
No, it's not.
It's lovely!


00:19:17.647 --> 00:19:20.230
I can feel it. It's freezing cold!


00:19:21.188 --> 00:19:23.938
- You come here!
- No. I'm gonna drink all the champagne.


00:19:24.022 --> 00:19:25.354
I don't care!


00:19:25.437 --> 00:19:27.687
God! Look
at what you're making me do.


00:20:56.812 --> 00:20:57.854
Oh, you're up.


00:20:58.979 --> 00:20:59.979
I, um...


00:21:01.521 --> 00:21:04.729
I'm so glad
you're feeling better. Where's the nurse?


00:21:05.562 --> 00:21:06.771
Dismissed.


00:21:08.562 --> 00:21:11.396
Took a swim, I see. After tennis?


00:21:12.729 --> 00:21:13.729
Yes.


00:21:14.854 --> 00:21:17.896
Well, go on. Dry your hair. Chop-chop.


00:21:18.854 --> 00:21:20.354
Are we going down for dinner?


00:21:21.729 --> 00:21:22.937
I am.


00:21:23.021 --> 00:21:26.521
You can see the concierge about
booking us on the early train tomorrow.


00:21:26.604 --> 00:21:28.395
And you can set about packing.


00:21:29.353 --> 00:21:30.561
Um, tomorrow?


00:21:30.645 --> 00:21:34.146
Billy is sailing for New York on Saturday.
We can catch the same boat.


00:21:34.729 --> 00:21:37.271
I'm sick to death of Europe.


00:21:42.812 --> 00:21:44.854
Don't look at me like a drowned rat.


00:21:44.937 --> 00:21:47.062
You'll get used to New York fast enough.


00:21:47.854 --> 00:21:50.146
Plenty of boys and excitement.


00:21:51.271 --> 00:21:52.603
All in your own class.


00:22:03.437 --> 00:22:06.062
Did you
really think people wouldn't talk?


00:22:07.312 --> 00:22:11.604
Oh, you're best out of it. Everyone knows
he nearly lost his mind after she died.


00:22:11.687 --> 00:22:14.354
It was all too sudden and tragic.


00:22:15.646 --> 00:22:18.478
Do you
honestly think he is in love with you?


00:22:20.186 --> 00:22:22.436
<i>It was a distraction, dear. That's it.</i>


00:22:23.936 --> 00:22:26.478
<i>We'll go away. We'll go to New York.</i>


00:22:27.478 --> 00:22:28.728
<i>You'll find your way.</i>


00:22:29.896 --> 00:22:31.271
You'll forget all about it.


00:22:32.562 --> 00:22:35.562
Trust me, you will forget all about it.


00:22:45.395 --> 00:22:46.520
Just a moment.


00:22:50.395 --> 00:22:53.145
Mrs. Van Hopper is leaving
and I have to go, too.


00:22:53.228 --> 00:22:55.228
- What are you talking about?
- Now. Today.


00:22:55.270 --> 00:22:57.436
I just wanted to say goodbye.


00:22:58.061 --> 00:22:59.354
Why haven't you told me before?


00:22:59.437 --> 00:23:01.354
Because she only decided it last night.


00:23:02.104 --> 00:23:05.311
And we're going to Paris with...
to meet her nephew.


00:23:05.395 --> 00:23:07.395
Then we go to Cherbourg
to sail to New York.


00:23:07.478 --> 00:23:11.436
All right. Listen, you mustn't cry.
Just give me a moment to think.


00:23:11.520 --> 00:23:12.520
I...


00:23:13.811 --> 00:23:17.061
I can't stay long.
She's expecting me downstairs.


00:23:20.978 --> 00:23:21.978
Come with me.


00:23:23.061 --> 00:23:24.061
What?


00:23:24.686 --> 00:23:25.686
To Manderley.


00:23:28.146 --> 00:23:31.145
What? As your secretary?


00:23:31.228 --> 00:23:33.103
No. No.


00:23:34.395 --> 00:23:35.645
As my wife.


00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:40.853
I'm asking you
to marry me, you little fool.


00:23:42.186 --> 00:23:43.811
I can't come to Manderley.


00:23:43.895 --> 00:23:47.061
Yes, you can.
You said you wanted to see the world.


00:23:47.145 --> 00:23:49.228
Manderley is the best part of it.


00:23:50.228 --> 00:23:53.186
Of course she's down there.
Where else is she?


00:23:53.270 --> 00:23:56.019
I've got to leave
in 20 minutes to catch the train.


00:23:56.769 --> 00:23:58.170
- I'll tell her.
- Do we have to go?


00:23:58.228 --> 00:24:00.520
Yes, we do.
I'm actually looking forward to this.


00:24:00.603 --> 00:24:02.228
That's exactly what I'm waiting for.


00:24:03.561 --> 00:24:04.603
Now, don't worry.


00:24:07.186 --> 00:24:08.311
Who is this now?


00:24:18.727 --> 00:24:22.477
This is the most wonderful news
I've ever heard in my life!


00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:24.411
Wait till I tell my friends,
I can't believe it!


00:24:24.435 --> 00:24:26.561
What are the plans?
I must know everything.


00:24:26.645 --> 00:24:27.561
The plans are settled.


00:24:27.645 --> 00:24:29.561
We'll marry here,
and honeymoon in Europe.


00:24:29.645 --> 00:24:31.645
And then home to Manderley.


00:24:31.728 --> 00:24:35.145
Oh, my goodness. Have you ever heard
of anything more romantic?


00:24:35.228 --> 00:24:36.478
- "Home to Manderley."
- Mmm.


00:24:36.561 --> 00:24:38.681
Oh, my goodness.
It's out of a fairy tale.


00:24:39.895 --> 00:24:44.144
All right. I'll go and make sure
your bags don't end up on the train.


00:24:44.227 --> 00:24:46.644
- Ah! Do hurry.
- You'll be fine.


00:24:46.727 --> 00:24:50.435
Yes, go along.
We have lots to talk about.


00:24:53.019 --> 00:24:56.561
Well, goodness gracious,
don't you work quickly?


00:24:57.895 --> 00:24:59.978
Have you been doing things you shouldn't?


00:25:00.811 --> 00:25:03.145
I don't know what you mean.


00:25:05.061 --> 00:25:07.769
Well, you don't have a family,
luckily, to explain it to.


00:25:08.477 --> 00:25:10.352
I wash my hands of it.


00:25:10.435 --> 00:25:13.102
Gonna have your work cut out for you
at Manderley.


00:25:13.185 --> 00:25:15.144
And, frankly,
I don't think you're up to it.


00:25:15.227 --> 00:25:17.894
- I can learn.
- Let me tell you something, honey.


00:25:20.352 --> 00:25:24.686
When you trap a man between your legs,
they don't stick around for long.


00:25:28.645 --> 00:25:30.353
Goodbye, Mrs. Van Hopper.


00:25:30.436 --> 00:25:33.519
He's only marrying you
because he doesn't want to go on living


00:25:33.602 --> 00:25:36.685
in that big old house with her ghost!


00:25:36.769 --> 00:25:38.102
I don't believe in ghosts.


00:25:59.602 --> 00:26:04.102
<i>♪ Come, all you fair and tender girls ♪</i>


00:26:04.185 --> 00:26:08.144
<i>♪ That flourish in your prime ♪</i>


00:26:08.227 --> 00:26:13.144
<i>♪ Beware, beware, keep your garden fair ♪</i>


00:26:13.685 --> 00:26:19.019
<i>♪ Let no man steal your thyme ♪</i>


00:26:19.102 --> 00:26:23.727
<i>♪ Let no man steal your thyme ♪</i>


00:26:25.977 --> 00:26:30.352
<i>♪ For when your thyme is past and gone ♪</i>


00:26:30.435 --> 00:26:34.519
<i>♪ He'll care no more for you ♪</i>


00:26:34.602 --> 00:26:39.602
<i>♪ And in the place your time was waste ♪</i>


00:26:41.144 --> 00:26:44.144
Oh, God.
I hate it when they do this.


00:26:50.018 --> 00:26:52.018
So much for keeping things quiet.


00:26:53.477 --> 00:26:55.435
You know how she is, sir.


00:26:55.519 --> 00:26:58.310
There's a way
things are done at Manderley.


00:26:59.644 --> 00:27:00.884
Darling, this is Frith.


00:27:01.310 --> 00:27:03.352
Hello.


00:27:09.601 --> 00:27:12.268
Let's do things
properly, shall we? There we go.


00:27:12.976 --> 00:27:14.976
- What are you doing?
- What? You don't like that?


00:27:15.059 --> 00:27:16.893
Up you go.


00:27:35.559 --> 00:27:37.476
Max, put me down.


00:27:44.684 --> 00:27:46.044
Oh.


00:27:48.851 --> 00:27:49.934
Mrs. Danvers.


00:27:51.060 --> 00:27:52.477
Welcome to Manderley.


00:27:53.602 --> 00:27:55.602
Hello. It's a pleasure. Oh!


00:28:03.184 --> 00:28:05.726
- Thank you. Thank you.
- Tea is ready.


00:28:08.351 --> 00:28:12.268
Danvers runs the house. Don't
worry, she's not as scary as she seems.


00:28:14.768 --> 00:28:16.643
Oh, Maxim, it's wonderful!


00:28:18.726 --> 00:28:19.810
Stop that.


00:28:21.269 --> 00:28:24.851
There he is. The wanderer returns.
Good to see you, Max.


00:28:24.934 --> 00:28:26.893
- And you, Frank.
- How was the trip?


00:28:27.518 --> 00:28:31.059
Was rather eventful, as it turns out.


00:28:31.143 --> 00:28:33.434
- Frank Crawley, Mrs. de Winter.
- It's a pleasure.


00:28:33.518 --> 00:28:34.768
Thank you. Hello.


00:28:34.851 --> 00:28:36.559
Frank's the estate manager.


00:28:36.643 --> 00:28:38.203
The place would fall apart without him.


00:28:38.268 --> 00:28:41.518
- Ah, no, no. He exaggerates.
- Ignore him.


00:28:42.351 --> 00:28:45.768
I hate to be a bore,
but I urgently need a few signatures.


00:28:46.351 --> 00:28:48.350
I'll have him back to you in a jiffy.


00:28:49.309 --> 00:28:50.768
- Shall we?
- Yes.


00:28:53.018 --> 00:28:54.184
Oh, uh...


00:28:54.268 --> 00:28:57.893
Danvers, show Mrs. de Winter the house.
Can you?


00:28:57.976 --> 00:28:59.643
Oh, that's all right. I'll wait.


00:28:59.726 --> 00:29:02.976
No, don't be silly.
Go on. I'll catch you up.


00:29:11.934 --> 00:29:15.225
The estate has been
in the family for over 300 years.


00:29:16.142 --> 00:29:18.143
It was originally a gift from Henry VIII.


00:29:20.559 --> 00:29:21.809
Extraordinary.


00:29:25.351 --> 00:29:27.910
If there are guests,
you may use the drawing room.


00:29:27.934 --> 00:29:30.851
Don't forget to tell Frith
to light the fires,


00:29:30.934 --> 00:29:35.643
but generally, Mr. de Winter prefers
to take his coffee here in the library.


00:29:36.933 --> 00:29:41.308
Glad you're here, Mrs. Danvers.
I'll never remember all this.


00:29:46.058 --> 00:29:49.768
Oh, I'm sure you won't disappoint him,
madam, if that's your concern.


00:29:50.851 --> 00:29:53.184
<i>The de Winter family
dates back to the Tudors.</i>


00:29:53.768 --> 00:29:55.934
And, um, who's that?


00:29:56.643 --> 00:30:00.059
That's Caroline de Winter.
Mr. de Winter's great aunt.


00:30:00.143 --> 00:30:01.622
She's very striking.


00:30:01.683 --> 00:30:05.933
Yes, and one of the first women
to qualify as a doctor in England.


00:30:07.558 --> 00:30:09.142
It's one of his favorites.


00:30:09.975 --> 00:30:11.655
Where does everyone sleep?


00:30:12.183 --> 00:30:16.308
Maids in the attic, men below stairs,
as in your other houses, I presume.


00:30:18.059 --> 00:30:20.351
Never even seen a house like this.


00:30:22.684 --> 00:30:25.351
Oh, I'm sorry.
I thought you'd been a lady's maid.


00:30:26.475 --> 00:30:28.850
The master bedroom
is now in the east wing.


00:30:44.475 --> 00:30:47.559
What a... pretty pattern.


00:30:49.351 --> 00:30:53.558
This is Clarice. She'll look after you
until your maid gets here.


00:30:54.183 --> 00:30:57.600
I don't have a maid,
but I'm sure I'll manage without one.


00:30:58.850 --> 00:31:00.975
Well, I think you'll find you need one.


00:31:02.142 --> 00:31:04.767
Perhaps Clarice could take the position.


00:31:06.642 --> 00:31:09.767
Oh! You can't see the sea from here.


00:31:09.850 --> 00:31:11.225
No, you can't.


00:31:12.517 --> 00:31:14.432
Should Mr. de Winter
ask for his old wardrobe,


00:31:14.516 --> 00:31:16.767
I'm afraid you must tell him
it wouldn't fit here.


00:31:16.850 --> 00:31:18.850
The rooms in this wing are much smaller.


00:31:19.850 --> 00:31:21.683
This wasn't his bedroom before?


00:31:21.767 --> 00:31:26.350
Oh, no. No. Mrs. de Winter's rooms
were in the west wing.


00:31:30.392 --> 00:31:33.725
Well, it's a lovely room.
Much too nice to stand empty.


00:31:34.392 --> 00:31:36.767
The guest rooms
are never empty for very long.


00:31:39.516 --> 00:31:42.891
We entertained a lot
when the late Mrs. de Winter was alive.


00:31:43.766 --> 00:31:45.767
The Manderley ball was quite an event.


00:31:47.808 --> 00:31:49.475
I'll leave you with Clarice.


00:31:58.100 --> 00:31:59.767
<i>Ask me a question.</i>


00:32:01.975 --> 00:32:03.308
<i>What sort of question?</i>


00:32:04.724 --> 00:32:06.432
<i>Anything.</i>


00:32:08.432 --> 00:32:10.307
<i>I have no secrets from you.</i>


00:32:11.641 --> 00:32:14.975
<i>Don't you think that's how it should be
now that we're married?</i>


00:32:15.767 --> 00:32:18.183
<i>All marriages have their secrets.</i>


00:32:22.308 --> 00:32:26.600
You can talk to me about her...
if you want.


00:32:37.266 --> 00:32:38.474
Good night, darling.


00:33:47.141 --> 00:33:48.391
Maxim?


00:34:28.682 --> 00:34:30.223
Leave him.


00:34:31.390 --> 00:34:33.390
It's dangerous to wake a sleepwalker.


00:35:50.015 --> 00:35:53.723
And nothing to worry about,
but the stables will need reroofing


00:35:53.806 --> 00:35:55.765
because the tiles are spoiled...


00:35:55.848 --> 00:35:57.056
Hmm.


00:35:57.140 --> 00:35:59.098
- Good morning, darling.
- Good morning.


00:35:59.181 --> 00:36:00.973
- Sleep well?
- Yes, not bad.


00:36:03.765 --> 00:36:04.765
Come.


00:36:06.181 --> 00:36:09.098
- How are you settling in?
- Very well, thank you.


00:36:09.181 --> 00:36:10.306
Good. Good.


00:36:11.556 --> 00:36:14.848
I'll...
see you up there, shall I?


00:36:14.931 --> 00:36:16.848
- Won't be a sec.
- Mrs. de Winter.


00:36:16.931 --> 00:36:17.931
Oh, Mr. Crawley.


00:36:19.431 --> 00:36:21.265
Frank. It's Frank.


00:36:24.640 --> 00:36:25.800
I should have got up earlier.


00:36:25.848 --> 00:36:28.765
- We could have had breakfast together.
- Oh, that's all right.


00:36:31.056 --> 00:36:32.764
Did you know you sleepwalk?


00:36:37.473 --> 00:36:38.973
Enjoy your breakfast.


00:37:01.972 --> 00:37:04.305
Jasper!


00:37:12.265 --> 00:37:15.265
Where are you going? Jasper!


00:37:17.556 --> 00:37:19.348
Jasper, where have you gone?


00:38:25.097 --> 00:38:26.264
Ow!


00:38:58.264 --> 00:39:00.388
I'm sorry to disturb you all...


00:39:01.054 --> 00:39:03.180
Clarice, have you seen Mr. de Winter?


00:39:03.264 --> 00:39:05.722
Do you have a plaster?
I've cut my hand.


00:39:05.805 --> 00:39:06.847
Let me see.


00:39:06.930 --> 00:39:09.764
- Really, it's nothing. I'm fine.
- Oh, my. One moment.


00:39:11.180 --> 00:39:15.180
Since you're here, madam, may I have
your approval for today's menus?


00:39:15.264 --> 00:39:16.347
Oh.


00:39:17.430 --> 00:39:21.014
Yes. Good.
Very suitable. Very nice indeed.


00:39:21.097 --> 00:39:24.179
- And the sauce for the roast veal?
- Yes, that looks excellent.


00:39:24.763 --> 00:39:26.804
No, but I've left it blank, you see?


00:39:27.971 --> 00:39:31.013
Mrs. de Winter was
most particular about her sauces.


00:39:33.264 --> 00:39:34.264
Right. Well, um...


00:39:35.222 --> 00:39:36.222
Uh...


00:39:37.055 --> 00:39:39.597
We'll have whatever Mrs. de Winter
would have had.


00:39:39.680 --> 00:39:40.680
Very well, madam.


00:39:43.680 --> 00:39:45.430
- There we go.
- Thank you very much.


00:40:19.763 --> 00:40:21.804
Is everything all right, darling?


00:40:21.888 --> 00:40:26.846
I was thinking of... ordering some
new undergarments from London.


00:40:28.221 --> 00:40:31.180
Something lacy and a nightgown.


00:40:33.555 --> 00:40:36.639
When have I ever complained
about what you wear?


00:40:45.971 --> 00:40:48.304
This is nice, isn't it?
Just us.


00:40:48.388 --> 00:40:51.013
It's almost like
we're back on our honeymoon.


00:40:52.346 --> 00:40:57.554
Oh, I miss it. Don't you?
Driving, the exploring, little cafes?


00:40:58.346 --> 00:41:01.305
Seeing some funny old hotel
and just staying there.


00:41:02.429 --> 00:41:04.388
That's not real life, darling.


00:41:06.138 --> 00:41:08.346
- Jasper! Jasper!
- I'll get him.


00:41:08.429 --> 00:41:11.221
No, just leave him.
He'll find his own way back.


00:41:11.304 --> 00:41:13.054
It's so steep. What if he falls?


00:41:13.138 --> 00:41:14.429
I said leave him!


00:41:17.846 --> 00:41:19.096
Jasper!


00:41:20.804 --> 00:41:21.846
Jasper!


00:41:23.929 --> 00:41:25.138
Jasper, come here!


00:41:31.013 --> 00:41:31.846
Jasper!


00:41:41.013 --> 00:41:42.013
Jasper!


00:41:45.054 --> 00:41:46.596
Jasper, come out of there.


00:42:14.263 --> 00:42:15.428
Jasper, come here.


00:42:17.137 --> 00:42:19.553
All right, get something to tie you with.


00:42:45.012 --> 00:42:46.303
Hello?


00:42:58.596 --> 00:43:00.846
There's nothing here, silly. Hey!


00:43:18.220 --> 00:43:19.053
I'm...


00:43:19.137 --> 00:43:21.970
I didn't realize that anyone lived here.


00:43:22.053 --> 00:43:25.054
No, I don't, do I?
Live up in the keeper's cottage.


00:43:25.846 --> 00:43:28.013
I've been digging
for shells since forenoon.


00:43:28.596 --> 00:43:30.720
Oh, you've been digging for shells? Huh?


00:43:31.553 --> 00:43:32.553
Um...


00:43:32.887 --> 00:43:34.303
No. I just, I...


00:43:35.512 --> 00:43:38.803
I needed something to tie my dog with.
I'll be out of your way.


00:43:38.887 --> 00:43:40.803
- He ain't yourn.
- Oh, no.


00:43:41.428 --> 00:43:43.428
- He's Mr. de Winter's dog.
- No.


00:43:43.512 --> 00:43:45.137
That's her dog.


00:43:47.053 --> 00:43:49.095
She don't come here no more.


00:43:49.762 --> 00:43:53.719
She... she gone into the sea, ain't she?


00:43:55.345 --> 00:43:56.678
She drowned.


00:44:00.012 --> 00:44:01.512
You ain't like her.


00:44:05.678 --> 00:44:08.137
Yes. Come on, Jasper.


00:44:09.220 --> 00:44:11.470
I never said nothin', did I?


00:44:12.762 --> 00:44:14.387
Come on, Jasper. Come on.


00:44:26.762 --> 00:44:29.387
I know why you didn't want
to come down here.


00:44:31.970 --> 00:44:33.303
How am I supposed to know?


00:44:33.970 --> 00:44:36.428
How am I supposed to know anything
if you don't tell me?


00:44:36.512 --> 00:44:39.053
- That's supposed to be locked.
- Someone was in there.


00:44:40.137 --> 00:44:43.302
Probably just the keeper's son,
Ben. He's harmless enough.


00:44:43.386 --> 00:44:44.552
Maxim, I...


00:45:08.427 --> 00:45:10.136
Oh, God!


00:45:13.219 --> 00:45:15.528
- That's in Italy.
- There he is.


00:45:15.552 --> 00:45:18.136
Oh, yes.
That was just after the wedding.


00:45:20.469 --> 00:45:21.970
What a nice plain frock.


00:45:23.428 --> 00:45:26.637
Look, Max was right.
You're not at all what I expected.


00:45:27.303 --> 00:45:29.762
And you're looking better, old man.


00:45:29.845 --> 00:45:30.970
Not so drawn.


00:45:31.053 --> 00:45:32.719
- Please.
- Bosh!


00:45:32.802 --> 00:45:36.011
Everyone knows you were
a perfect wreck six months ago.


00:45:37.302 --> 00:45:39.802
Here, Granny, have you seen these?


00:45:39.886 --> 00:45:41.927
- Look, aren't they lovely?
- Ah.


00:45:42.011 --> 00:45:43.719
Goodness! Yes.


00:45:43.802 --> 00:45:45.927
So,
these were from our wedding.


00:45:46.511 --> 00:45:49.219
What's all this
I hear about you not hunting?


00:45:49.969 --> 00:45:51.595
Oh, no, I'm afraid I don't ride.


00:45:51.678 --> 00:45:54.887
Oh, but you must!
Or you'll miss out on all the fun.


00:45:54.970 --> 00:45:56.427
Come and stay. I can teach you.


00:45:56.511 --> 00:45:58.302
Finest horsewoman in the county.


00:45:58.386 --> 00:45:59.969
Do dry up, Giles.


00:46:00.052 --> 00:46:03.677
It might shock my sister
that not everyone shares her idea of fun.


00:46:03.761 --> 00:46:07.386
Whatever her idea of fun,
she certainly deserves to have some.


00:46:07.469 --> 00:46:11.636
Well, actually, I've been
thinking I might revive the ball.


00:46:14.427 --> 00:46:15.761
- Huh.
- Oh!


00:46:16.594 --> 00:46:18.927
Hmm, what a marvelous idea.


00:46:19.677 --> 00:46:21.552
That's not something we discussed.


00:46:22.136 --> 00:46:24.594
Oh,
don't be so damn miserable.


00:46:25.177 --> 00:46:26.594
You used to love it.


00:46:27.177 --> 00:46:29.719
You can hold it
in honor of your new bride.


00:46:33.802 --> 00:46:34.802
Fine.


00:46:36.261 --> 00:46:38.136
Well, that's settled, then.


00:46:38.219 --> 00:46:40.969
- To our new hostess.
- Yeah. To our new hostess.


00:46:42.469 --> 00:46:45.260
Are you staying at Manderley, dear?


00:46:45.676 --> 00:46:46.716
She lives here.


00:46:46.760 --> 00:46:49.427
- Remember, Granny?
- Granny, we introduced you.


00:46:49.511 --> 00:46:51.427
She's Maxim's wife.


00:46:53.219 --> 00:46:54.927
No, she is not.


00:47:02.261 --> 00:47:05.594
She's not Maxim's wife.


00:47:07.136 --> 00:47:10.301
What a silly notion.


00:47:10.385 --> 00:47:15.510
Uh, well, it's...
good news about the ball, uh...


00:47:16.135 --> 00:47:17.801
It's been far too long.


00:47:17.885 --> 00:47:19.844
I don't remember you.


00:47:20.511 --> 00:47:22.219
Oh, no, I...


00:47:22.886 --> 00:47:25.177
We haven't met before.


00:47:26.386 --> 00:47:29.886
- Maxim, who is this child?
- Ow!


00:47:29.969 --> 00:47:32.761
- Oh, Christ.
- All right, let's get Granny home.


00:47:32.844 --> 00:47:35.010
What have
you done with Rebecca?


00:47:35.093 --> 00:47:36.801
- Leave it.
- No, I've got it!


00:47:36.885 --> 00:47:38.725
I want to see Rebecca.
Leave me alone!


00:47:38.760 --> 00:47:42.426
She just gets a little...
it's the time of day, and the weather...


00:47:44.593 --> 00:47:47.314
- Oh, my! Get her in the car.
- I just want to...


00:47:47.386 --> 00:47:48.927
You go and talk to her.


00:47:49.011 --> 00:47:51.011
Let's get in the car, Granny. Come on.


00:47:51.094 --> 00:47:54.219
This is from the flower room.
I hope that's all right.


00:47:54.302 --> 00:47:56.022
- Thank you.
- I apologize.


00:47:56.052 --> 00:47:59.426
I'd forgotten how fond
our grandmother was of Rebecca.


00:47:59.510 --> 00:48:00.593
I'm fine.


00:48:00.676 --> 00:48:03.968
She was just
one of those bloody annoying people.


00:48:04.051 --> 00:48:09.926
Irresistible to everybody. The men, women,
children, animals.


00:48:10.010 --> 00:48:12.843
Us mere mortals couldn't hope to compete.


00:48:44.718 --> 00:48:46.636
- Sir.
- Why is he crying?


00:48:46.719 --> 00:48:49.926
Sir, one of the porcelain pieces
is missing from the morning room,


00:48:50.010 --> 00:48:52.343
and now Danvers
is calling for the boy's dismissal.


00:48:52.426 --> 00:48:53.706
- But it wasn't...
- Which piece?


00:48:53.760 --> 00:48:54.801
We're not sure, sir.


00:48:55.676 --> 00:48:56.676
Danvers!


00:48:57.593 --> 00:49:00.260
- Is everything all right?
- Yes, it's fine.


00:49:00.343 --> 00:49:02.968
Something's just gone missing
from the morning room.


00:49:03.051 --> 00:49:06.093
- Danvers!
- What is it? What's gone missing?


00:49:08.676 --> 00:49:10.801
What makes you think Robert took it?


00:49:11.759 --> 00:49:13.842
The Dresden is extremely valuable, sir.


00:49:13.925 --> 00:49:16.277
- But it wasn't me!
- That piece is worth £100.


00:49:16.301 --> 00:49:19.261
- Sir, I find it most unlikely...
- Then who, Frith?


00:49:19.926 --> 00:49:23.260
The between maid isn't allowed
in the morning room. I do it.


00:49:23.885 --> 00:49:26.010
When Mrs. de Winter
was alive, we did it together.


00:49:26.093 --> 00:49:28.093
- All Frith is saying...
- It was me.


00:49:32.301 --> 00:49:35.176
I broke it. It broke.


00:49:36.509 --> 00:49:38.342
It was an accident. It fell.


00:49:41.967 --> 00:49:44.218
Well, there we go.


00:49:44.801 --> 00:49:46.468
Robert, you're off the hook.


00:49:51.593 --> 00:49:53.301
Where are the pieces, madam?


00:49:54.885 --> 00:49:57.218
In the bureau drawer at the back.


00:49:58.093 --> 00:50:00.176
Send them to London.
See if anything can be done.


00:50:00.260 --> 00:50:01.459
Certainly, sir.


00:50:01.509 --> 00:50:04.884
And may I suggest,
should anything like this happen again,


00:50:04.967 --> 00:50:06.759
that Mrs. de Winter tell me herself.


00:50:08.384 --> 00:50:09.967
If we're all quite finished?


00:52:06.633 --> 00:52:07.633
Oh, Frank.


00:52:08.424 --> 00:52:09.424
Mrs. de Winter.


00:52:10.759 --> 00:52:12.884
I thought you'd
gone up to London with Max.


00:52:13.550 --> 00:52:14.675
He's in London?


00:52:15.259 --> 00:52:18.092
Yeah. Taking care of some paperwork.


00:52:19.134 --> 00:52:21.717
He asked me to put a padlock on.
I nearly locked you in.


00:52:23.384 --> 00:52:24.425
It's a shame.


00:52:26.259 --> 00:52:27.758
This place going to ruin.


00:52:29.049 --> 00:52:32.716
Well... no boat now.


00:52:35.341 --> 00:52:36.841
Max doesn't like to sail.


00:52:53.383 --> 00:52:54.674
Ben said she drowned.


00:52:56.508 --> 00:52:59.424
I'm sorry. I assumed you knew.


00:53:00.674 --> 00:53:02.591
- No.
- Ah, it's...


00:53:03.341 --> 00:53:04.674
It was brutal weather.


00:53:05.883 --> 00:53:08.383
Even for her. She was an excellent sailor.


00:53:09.092 --> 00:53:10.342
The boat went down.


00:53:11.842 --> 00:53:13.259
They never recovered it.


00:53:14.342 --> 00:53:18.091
She washed up
in Edgcumbe some... two months later.


00:53:18.799 --> 00:53:21.674
Two months? My God!


00:53:23.049 --> 00:53:24.049
Poor Maxim.


00:53:24.841 --> 00:53:28.174
Drove him down there myself
to identify the body.


00:53:30.424 --> 00:53:33.633
You know, you really
mustn't dwell on the past.


00:53:33.716 --> 00:53:36.216
You're so good for Max.
He's a changed man.


00:53:38.175 --> 00:53:39.925
She must have been so afraid.


00:53:41.633 --> 00:53:42.924
Out there alone.


00:53:44.133 --> 00:53:45.924
She wasn't afraid of anything.


00:53:53.424 --> 00:53:57.341
Can I ask you something, Frank?
And promise to tell me the truth.


00:53:57.424 --> 00:54:01.008
Hardly fair.
Don't know what you're gonna ask me.


00:54:02.508 --> 00:54:04.424
Was Rebecca very beautiful?


00:54:08.633 --> 00:54:09.633
Yes.


00:54:12.758 --> 00:54:14.341
Yes, I suppose she was...


00:54:15.549 --> 00:54:18.674
the most beautiful
creature I ever saw in my life.


00:55:14.383 --> 00:55:16.463
It is beautiful, isn't it?


00:55:18.299 --> 00:55:20.090
I keep it just the way it was.


00:55:21.340 --> 00:55:23.882
It's as if she'd just
gone out for a while.


00:55:24.923 --> 00:55:26.298
You startled me.


00:55:28.215 --> 00:55:29.798
This was her favorite.


00:55:32.632 --> 00:55:34.716
I laid it out for her that night.


00:55:42.841 --> 00:55:44.298
Go on, hold it.


00:55:45.882 --> 00:55:46.882
Touch it.


00:55:52.132 --> 00:55:56.840
She wouldn't have a lady's maid, you know.
"I don't want anyone but you, Danny."


00:55:59.090 --> 00:56:00.923
Do you see how tall she was?


00:56:05.216 --> 00:56:08.715
Hmm. She could wear
anything with a figure like hers.


00:56:11.340 --> 00:56:15.132
I'd brush her hair for her every evening.


00:56:18.507 --> 00:56:20.882
"Come on, Danny, hair drill," she'd say.


00:56:22.382 --> 00:56:24.007
I'd stand behind her...


00:56:25.132 --> 00:56:28.548
and brush away for 20 minutes at a time.


00:56:29.965 --> 00:56:33.173
That great mass of dark hair.


00:56:37.757 --> 00:56:39.007
He joined in.


00:56:40.923 --> 00:56:42.798
He loved to do that for her.


00:56:44.507 --> 00:56:47.840
They'd be dressing for dinner,
guests waiting downstairs.


00:56:47.923 --> 00:56:50.757
"Harder, Max, harder!"


00:56:50.840 --> 00:56:53.090
And he'd roar with laughter.


00:56:55.090 --> 00:56:57.047
He was always laughing back then.


00:57:03.007 --> 00:57:04.507
Does he brush your hair?


00:57:06.048 --> 00:57:07.048
No.


00:57:09.882 --> 00:57:15.048
Mrs. Danvers, does Mr. de Winter
ask you to keep the room like this?


00:57:15.132 --> 00:57:16.548
He doesn't have to.


00:57:17.632 --> 00:57:19.007
She's still here.


00:57:21.007 --> 00:57:22.089
Can you feel her?


00:57:24.381 --> 00:57:27.089
I wonder what she's thinking about you.


00:57:27.589 --> 00:57:31.673
Taking her husband and... using her name.


00:57:34.715 --> 00:57:37.007
- I'm sure she'd want him to be happy.
- Happy?


00:57:37.090 --> 00:57:38.798
No, he'll never be happy.


00:57:42.007 --> 00:57:43.798
She was the love of his life.


00:58:15.506 --> 00:58:16.506
Maxim?


00:58:32.507 --> 00:58:34.215
Good morning, madam.


00:58:34.922 --> 00:58:38.589
Oh, dear! You've been scratchin'.


00:59:16.172 --> 00:59:18.006
Have we missed ya?


00:59:22.589 --> 00:59:25.796
Hello! You must be the new Mrs. de Winter.


00:59:26.380 --> 00:59:28.172
Uh, I think there's been a mistake.


00:59:28.756 --> 00:59:31.547
- Mr. de Winter's in London.
- He's left you on your own?


00:59:32.297 --> 00:59:34.797
Isn't he afraid some bounder
might come and carry you off?


00:59:35.381 --> 00:59:37.714
I'm Jack Favell. How do you do?


00:59:41.464 --> 00:59:42.464
Um...


00:59:43.089 --> 00:59:45.506
Well, did you want to leave your card?


00:59:46.464 --> 00:59:48.755
And too polite to tell me to bugger off.


00:59:48.838 --> 00:59:50.255
You are a sweetheart.


00:59:50.338 --> 00:59:53.046
Not to worry.
I just popped by to see Danny.


00:59:53.130 --> 00:59:54.880
She's invited me for tea.


00:59:55.671 --> 00:59:58.839
- I'm horribly early, though.
- Mrs. Danvers?


00:59:59.422 --> 01:00:01.672
That's why I thought
I'd better hover around out here,


01:00:01.756 --> 01:00:04.047
otherwise I might
get a smack on the wrist.


01:00:10.756 --> 01:00:13.671
Mr. Favell? Where are you going?


01:00:13.755 --> 01:00:15.963
Charlie, come on.


01:00:16.046 --> 01:00:17.939
- Excuse me, Mr. Favell!
- Coming, sir.


01:00:19.546 --> 01:00:21.213
Phillippa! Come on in, Charlie.


01:00:21.296 --> 01:00:24.088
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Stand down.


01:00:24.171 --> 01:00:25.671
- Easy, Starlight.
- Steady.


01:00:26.256 --> 01:00:29.172
You've too much energy.
They've been neglecting you.


01:00:29.256 --> 01:00:30.297
That's not a surprise.


01:00:30.881 --> 01:00:33.839
Rebecca was the only one
who could handle you, wasn't she, old boy?


01:00:33.922 --> 01:00:34.922
Yes.


01:00:35.547 --> 01:00:36.714
You knew Rebecca?


01:00:38.755 --> 01:00:41.255
She's my cousin. Was.


01:00:43.838 --> 01:00:44.838
That's it.


01:00:45.380 --> 01:00:47.130
Let's take one of the horses
out for a turn.


01:00:47.213 --> 01:00:50.046
Oh, no. I really... I don't know how.


01:00:50.130 --> 01:00:54.088
Well, I can teach you.
Or have you something better to be doing?


01:00:54.796 --> 01:00:56.922
- How do I...
- On three, swing your leg over.


01:00:57.006 --> 01:00:58.440
- Ready?
- Do you...


01:00:58.464 --> 01:00:59.797
One, two, three.


01:01:01.547 --> 01:01:04.630
- Can you give me a stirrup? All right.
- All right.


01:01:04.713 --> 01:01:05.796
Are you...


01:01:07.963 --> 01:01:10.630
We won't go too fast.


01:01:15.921 --> 01:01:17.046
That's it.


01:01:20.005 --> 01:01:21.130
How do you feel?


01:01:24.505 --> 01:01:27.255
- Right, now you take the reins.
- Oh, all right.


01:01:27.838 --> 01:01:29.421
- Be nice and loose.
- Yeah.


01:01:29.505 --> 01:01:32.046
And low. That's it.


01:01:32.130 --> 01:01:34.046
- Got it.
- Right here on your lap.


01:01:34.880 --> 01:01:37.880
Now, very important. Squeeze the thighs.


01:01:38.713 --> 01:01:41.338
- Let the beast know you're there.
- Mmm-hmm.


01:01:41.421 --> 01:01:43.755
You're gonna be
wickedly sore this evening.


01:01:44.296 --> 01:01:46.380
- Now just move with me. Ready?
- Mmm-hmm.


01:01:46.463 --> 01:01:47.503
All right.


01:01:50.795 --> 01:01:52.504
<i>Darling, may I ask you something?</i>


01:01:53.170 --> 01:01:55.921
Has Max ever talked to you
about the accident?


01:01:58.713 --> 01:02:01.796
And he never mentioned
Rebecca's trip to London that day?


01:02:03.088 --> 01:02:04.088
No.


01:02:05.421 --> 01:02:07.338
No, he won't speak of it at all.


01:02:10.255 --> 01:02:14.921
So, you don't know if he saw her
when she got back that night,


01:02:16.295 --> 01:02:17.837
before she took the boat out?


01:02:18.962 --> 01:02:19.962
No.


01:02:20.962 --> 01:02:21.962
Hmm.


01:02:26.130 --> 01:02:28.588
There's something she wanted to tell me.


01:02:29.505 --> 01:02:31.046
Something very important.


01:02:35.005 --> 01:02:37.005
And not knowing what it was...


01:02:40.129 --> 01:02:42.045
That's really been a hard thing.


01:02:46.170 --> 01:02:48.837
I'm not doing
my roguish image any good, am I?


01:02:51.629 --> 01:02:53.713
You should come back and ask Maxim.


01:02:54.213 --> 01:02:55.213
Well, I would.


01:02:58.213 --> 01:03:00.505
But I'm afraid I'm a little bit banned
from visiting.


01:03:02.005 --> 01:03:05.420
In fact, it's best if you don't mention
my being here at all today.


01:03:05.504 --> 01:03:08.004
I... I thought you were friends.


01:03:08.920 --> 01:03:10.004
Not really, no.


01:03:13.879 --> 01:03:17.129
And I would hate for either one of us


01:03:17.920 --> 01:03:20.962
to be on the receiving end
of that famous temper of his.


01:03:21.045 --> 01:03:22.606
I don't know what you're talking about.


01:03:25.130 --> 01:03:27.255
Well, it is still early days.


01:03:32.254 --> 01:03:35.754
Well, I better not keep Danny waiting.
You know how she is.


01:04:06.670 --> 01:04:08.045
Why did you invite him?


01:04:10.295 --> 01:04:11.295
Jack Favell.


01:04:12.254 --> 01:04:13.712
You asked him for tea,


01:04:14.295 --> 01:04:17.878
knowing full well Mr. de Winter
has banned him from the property.


01:04:18.586 --> 01:04:20.629
There must be some mistake, madam.


01:04:21.295 --> 01:04:24.212
I haven't seen Mr. Favell for over a year.


01:04:55.962 --> 01:04:56.879
Hello, Frith.


01:04:56.962 --> 01:05:00.420
Hello, sir. Mr. Favell
has made an unannounced visit.


01:05:05.295 --> 01:05:07.254
<i>I don't care
what she told Frith!</i>


01:05:07.336 --> 01:05:10.419
<i>Mr. Favell told me
that she invited him here.</i>


01:05:10.503 --> 01:05:14.003
And I suppose Mrs. Danvers forced you
to go riding with him, did she?


01:05:14.086 --> 01:05:15.419
No, I can explain!


01:05:15.503 --> 01:05:18.254
- Explain what?
- I was going to tell you, I was.


01:05:18.337 --> 01:05:21.795
Want to tell me how you
dragged him down to the boathouse?


01:05:23.295 --> 01:05:26.420
Parade your
fancy new night clothes for him?


01:05:26.504 --> 01:05:28.170
How could you even think that?


01:05:28.754 --> 01:05:33.503
I'd never have let him on the property
if I'd known it would upset you, Maxim.


01:05:34.169 --> 01:05:36.878
Please. I love you.


01:05:40.878 --> 01:05:42.044
Oh, do you?


01:05:42.628 --> 01:05:44.419
Mrs. Danvers invited him here.


01:05:44.503 --> 01:05:47.462
I don't wanna hear
another word about Danvers!


01:06:12.003 --> 01:06:13.003
Come in.


01:06:18.587 --> 01:06:19.629
Mrs. Danvers.


01:06:20.711 --> 01:06:22.336
I've come to give you your notice.


01:06:25.836 --> 01:06:28.128
Has Mr. de Winter agreed to this?


01:06:28.211 --> 01:06:29.586
The decision is mine.


01:06:35.961 --> 01:06:37.211
You see...


01:06:38.753 --> 01:06:41.753
I looked after Rebecca
when she was a little girl.


01:06:42.586 --> 01:06:45.585
We came here together
when she was first married.


01:06:48.669 --> 01:06:50.003
I was her friend.


01:06:52.378 --> 01:06:54.336
Someone to share her secrets.


01:06:57.044 --> 01:06:58.836
Bond like that can't be broke.


01:06:59.586 --> 01:07:02.794
Can't be replaced.
I was wrong to expect that from you.


01:07:05.836 --> 01:07:09.418
Well, you'll find another house.


01:07:12.293 --> 01:07:13.335
No.


01:07:14.043 --> 01:07:19.711
We women, we can either marry
or go into service,


01:07:19.794 --> 01:07:22.211
and I'm too old for either.


01:07:23.878 --> 01:07:26.794
Well, we'll make sure
that you're provided for.


01:07:26.878 --> 01:07:28.628
Oh, it's not about money. It's...


01:07:29.294 --> 01:07:33.169
This wasn't a job for me.
Rebecca was my life.


01:07:36.793 --> 01:07:37.793
Yes.


01:07:38.335 --> 01:07:40.085
I'm sorry if I failed you.


01:07:40.168 --> 01:07:41.585
I didn't mean to let you down.


01:07:41.668 --> 01:07:45.169
It was just you seemed
so set on doing things your own way.


01:07:46.294 --> 01:07:48.336
No. This is all very new to me.


01:07:48.961 --> 01:07:50.711
The house, the staff...


01:07:51.753 --> 01:07:56.961
I just... I think that Mr. de Winter
hoped that you'd help me.


01:07:58.835 --> 01:08:00.668
You didn't ask for my help.


01:08:07.335 --> 01:08:08.335
Well...


01:08:11.002 --> 01:08:12.627
what if I asked for it now?


01:08:47.877 --> 01:08:49.168
I'm sorry.


01:08:50.710 --> 01:08:54.085
I was an idiot. It's not your fault.


01:08:56.377 --> 01:08:57.668
I know it wasn't.


01:09:08.668 --> 01:09:10.043
I'm so sorry.


01:09:28.002 --> 01:09:29.002
Okay.


01:09:33.793 --> 01:09:37.792
Very good, madam. Perfect.
I'll have them printed at once.


01:09:37.876 --> 01:09:40.626
Oh, and we must let
Voce in London know before Friday


01:09:40.709 --> 01:09:42.377
if you wish them to make your costume.


01:09:42.460 --> 01:09:45.960
<i>Yes. I'm afraid
I'm drawing a bit of a blank there.</i>


01:09:46.043 --> 01:09:47.043
<i>Oh.</i>


01:09:48.002 --> 01:09:52.043
Well, you'll be
the most important lady at the ball.


01:09:52.127 --> 01:09:55.627
- So, choose something with that in mind.
- Yes.


01:09:56.793 --> 01:09:58.168
Oh, be confident.


01:09:59.085 --> 01:10:01.376
Let them see your natural beauty.


01:10:04.667 --> 01:10:06.042
Madam?


01:10:06.751 --> 01:10:09.042
If it's not too forward of me...


01:10:10.085 --> 01:10:13.918
Mrs. Danvers said you'd
not picked out what to wear yet, and...


01:10:15.168 --> 01:10:17.168
I wondered if you'd want an idea.


01:10:18.293 --> 01:10:21.543
Yes, please, anything. Sit down.


01:10:21.627 --> 01:10:22.627
Um...


01:10:23.710 --> 01:10:27.084
Just... the old paintings in the gallery.


01:10:27.917 --> 01:10:31.001
I always thought they'd make
the most beautiful costume.


01:10:31.709 --> 01:10:34.292
<i>Especially the lady in the red dress.</i>


01:10:40.210 --> 01:10:41.210
Brilliant choice.


01:10:42.585 --> 01:10:43.960
Clarice informed me.


01:10:44.043 --> 01:10:48.168
And if I may say so,
one worthy of the lady of this house.


01:10:53.626 --> 01:10:54.959
I do apologize.


01:11:24.042 --> 01:11:26.376
Right. Will you take
this down to Mrs. Danvers?


01:11:26.459 --> 01:11:28.018
- Make sure she has everything.
- Right.


01:11:28.042 --> 01:11:30.402
- Thank you very much.
- And if you go through to the house.


01:11:30.459 --> 01:11:31.542
- Oh, sorry.
- I'm sorry!


01:11:31.626 --> 01:11:33.626
- Welcome.
- Are you quite all right?


01:11:33.709 --> 01:11:36.292
- Yes. There's bit of a wind, Frank.
- Well, yes.


01:11:36.376 --> 01:11:38.643
- Hope it doesn't rain.
- It'll come to nothing, I'm sure.


01:11:38.667 --> 01:11:39.667
Oh, dear.


01:11:58.626 --> 01:12:02.084
- What? Hands off! Don't!
- Can't I just see?


01:12:02.167 --> 01:12:04.333
No, you'll ruin the surprise.


01:12:04.416 --> 01:12:06.166
You know I don't like surprises.


01:12:06.250 --> 01:12:09.292
Well, you'll like this one.


01:12:10.209 --> 01:12:11.584
You won't recognize me.


01:12:12.126 --> 01:12:13.751
Hmm?


01:12:15.834 --> 01:12:17.042
I'm so proud of you.


01:12:21.959 --> 01:12:24.417
Now, don't you leave me
down there too long.


01:12:24.501 --> 01:12:26.584
Then get out so I can get ready.


01:12:45.001 --> 01:12:48.126
<i>♪ Every time it rains, it rains ♪</i>


01:12:48.209 --> 01:12:50.459
<i>♪ Pennies from heaven ♪</i>


01:12:50.542 --> 01:12:53.458
<i>♪ Don't you know each cloud contains... ♪</i>


01:12:54.041 --> 01:12:55.375
- Here you go.
- Oh...


01:12:56.166 --> 01:12:57.458
no, I couldn't.


01:12:57.541 --> 01:12:59.958
Don't be silly.
It's all right, I won't tell anyone.


01:13:03.041 --> 01:13:04.958
No, go away! You can't come in!


01:13:05.041 --> 01:13:07.209
The guests are arriving, ma'am.


01:13:07.792 --> 01:13:09.792
Oh, all right. Let's greet them.


01:13:10.417 --> 01:13:13.334
Please inform them
madam will be down presently.


01:13:15.084 --> 01:13:16.083
Very good.


01:13:18.833 --> 01:13:21.416
- What are you doing lurking over here?
- Nothing.


01:13:21.500 --> 01:13:24.250
- It's just like old times, isn't it?
- Mmm, it's good.


01:13:24.333 --> 01:13:25.375
Where's your outfit?


01:13:25.458 --> 01:13:27.708
- This is my outfit, Giles.
- It's marvelous.


01:13:27.791 --> 01:13:29.416
Palaver!
Oh, champagne.


01:13:29.500 --> 01:13:31.958
- Late as usual.
- So, what's your excuse?


01:13:32.875 --> 01:13:34.756
Tree down across the drive.
Had to get it moved.


01:13:34.834 --> 01:13:37.376
No, no, for this.


01:13:37.459 --> 01:13:39.292
But I wear it every year, mate.


01:13:53.916 --> 01:13:56.208
All right. Finally. Hey, here she comes.


01:14:20.958 --> 01:14:22.291
How do you do, Mr. de Winter?


01:14:36.333 --> 01:14:37.916
Is this some kind of joke?


01:14:39.666 --> 01:14:43.000
Of course not.
It's the painting. I thought...


01:14:43.083 --> 01:14:44.125
Go and change.


01:14:46.541 --> 01:14:48.041
What is it? What have I...


01:14:48.125 --> 01:14:51.000
Go and change now.


01:14:53.375 --> 01:14:54.374
I don't understand.


01:14:54.457 --> 01:14:56.582
- What have I done wrong?
- I said now!


01:15:10.208 --> 01:15:13.833
I'm sorry. Please, madam, I never knew.


01:15:13.916 --> 01:15:16.000
It was Mrs. Danvers' idea.


01:15:24.707 --> 01:15:27.499
Rebecca wore this before, didn't she?


01:15:27.582 --> 01:15:33.541
Mrs. Danvers said he'd be
so pleased and you'd be so pleased.


01:15:40.875 --> 01:15:41.875
Hold that.


01:15:44.040 --> 01:15:47.290
- That's most unfortunate.
- It was uncanny, wasn't it?


01:15:55.207 --> 01:15:58.540
- No, I can't.
- Oh, bosh! Darling, you have to.


01:15:59.415 --> 01:16:00.416
No.


01:16:01.583 --> 01:16:03.375
It's not as bad as all that.


01:16:04.375 --> 01:16:08.582
You don't understand, I can't.
Not after this. Not after what I've done.


01:16:08.665 --> 01:16:10.499
How were you to know?


01:16:10.582 --> 01:16:14.582
Now, wash your face, and I'll find you
something to wear, all right?


01:16:15.499 --> 01:16:16.915
I should've known.


01:16:17.499 --> 01:16:20.124
- I should never have worn it.
- Pull yourself together.


01:16:20.207 --> 01:16:22.874
You can sit up here all night
feeling sorry for yourself,


01:16:22.957 --> 01:16:26.999
or you can come downstairs with me
and have a good old laugh about it, hmm?


01:16:33.832 --> 01:16:35.124
His face...


01:16:37.457 --> 01:16:40.540
He wouldn't have spoken like that to her.


01:16:41.790 --> 01:16:45.790
You're very different people,
and that's nothing to be ashamed of.


01:16:48.374 --> 01:16:49.374
- Okay.
- Come on.


01:16:49.457 --> 01:16:52.415
You're not on the continent.
Let's have a stiff upper lip.


01:16:52.499 --> 01:16:54.249
- What?
- Oh, yes.


01:16:55.832 --> 01:16:56.831
This'll do.


01:16:59.999 --> 01:17:01.249
I'll be all right.


01:17:02.332 --> 01:17:03.457
Good show.


01:17:05.332 --> 01:17:06.832
- I'll see you downstairs.
- Yes.


01:17:06.915 --> 01:17:08.082
- Yes?
- Yes.


01:17:41.290 --> 01:17:43.124
Nothing would make me happy...


01:17:44.165 --> 01:17:47.248
Lord Crowan, Lady Crowan,
may I present Mrs. de Winter.


01:17:47.331 --> 01:17:50.123
Oh, rotten luck about
your frock not turning up.


01:17:50.206 --> 01:17:52.039
- Yes.
- Oh, never mind.


01:17:52.123 --> 01:17:53.206
You look lovely,


01:17:53.289 --> 01:17:56.331
and far more comfortable
than I am in this ridiculous getup.


01:17:56.414 --> 01:17:58.540
Oh, don't be silly, darling.
You look divine.


01:18:00.415 --> 01:18:02.707
- Maxim, I...
- This whole idea was a mistake.


01:18:02.790 --> 01:18:04.999
I should never have brought you back here.


01:19:03.414 --> 01:19:07.789
There are sailors and soldiers
returned from the war.


01:19:07.873 --> 01:19:09.873
This ain't no place for you, miss.


01:19:09.956 --> 01:19:14.414
Who bravely have fought
in their country's cause.


01:19:14.998 --> 01:19:20.206
To come home, to be starved,
best stayed where they was...


01:19:38.164 --> 01:19:42.414
<i>♪ A woman is a branchy tree ♪</i>


01:19:42.498 --> 01:19:46.581
<i>♪ And man's a clinging vine ♪</i>


01:19:46.664 --> 01:19:51.497
<i>♪ And from her branches carelessly ♪</i>


01:19:51.580 --> 01:19:56.706
<i>♪ He'll take what he can find ♪</i>


01:20:03.164 --> 01:20:07.789
Rebecca! Rebecca! Rebecca!


01:20:39.497 --> 01:20:40.705
Maxim?


01:20:59.748 --> 01:21:01.330
There, do you see now?


01:21:03.622 --> 01:21:05.038
You'll never replace her.


01:21:05.122 --> 01:21:07.288
- You can't replace her.
- You did this.


01:21:09.247 --> 01:21:12.288
- You've been against me from the start.
- No.


01:21:12.372 --> 01:21:15.747
- I was helping you.
- You tricked me. You planned this.


01:21:16.330 --> 01:21:21.456
You and I both know
you are nothing. You're worthless.


01:21:21.539 --> 01:21:24.998
Not worthy of him
and not worthy of this house.


01:21:25.913 --> 01:21:28.413
He'll never love you.


01:21:28.497 --> 01:21:30.038
And why should he?


01:21:31.580 --> 01:21:32.622
He did.


01:21:32.705 --> 01:21:35.497
No, he can't love you
because you're not her.


01:21:37.038 --> 01:21:38.413
You should've seen her.


01:21:38.497 --> 01:21:42.622
At 16 years old,
on her father's horse, a huge brute,


01:21:42.705 --> 01:21:44.747
but she mastered him.


01:21:44.830 --> 01:21:49.663
By the time she finished with him,
he was nothing but froth and blood.


01:21:51.997 --> 01:21:54.955
I've let her down,
allowing you here for so long.


01:21:56.163 --> 01:21:57.580
She won't stand for it.


01:21:57.663 --> 01:21:59.997
"I'll see you in hell, Danny!
I'll see you in hell first!"


01:22:00.080 --> 01:22:03.372
But Rebecca's dead!
She's dead!


01:22:04.080 --> 01:22:07.580
He'll leave you, he'll divorce you.
And then what'll you do?


01:22:08.163 --> 01:22:09.163
I'll just go.


01:22:09.747 --> 01:22:12.455
You'll go? Go where?


01:22:13.122 --> 01:22:14.954
You can't remarry now.


01:22:15.704 --> 01:22:20.705
You certainly can't look after a house.
You don't have any family to support you.


01:22:26.580 --> 01:22:27.622
It's all right.


01:22:28.872 --> 01:22:31.913
I know how you feel.
It's not as bad as all that.


01:22:33.580 --> 01:22:34.830
It'll be very quick.


01:22:36.663 --> 01:22:40.371
Don't be scared. It's all for the best.


01:22:41.787 --> 01:22:43.746
No one wants you here.


01:22:49.372 --> 01:22:51.288
Frith! Robert! Come quickly.


01:22:51.372 --> 01:22:53.705
A trawler's run aground.
Get the coast guard.


01:22:53.788 --> 01:22:55.997
- They're on the way, sir.
- Maxim.


01:23:18.872 --> 01:23:20.747
What's he doin' down there?


01:23:25.247 --> 01:23:26.830
Daniel, wait for me.


01:23:28.662 --> 01:23:31.704
Move on, now. Get up, now.
That's it.


01:23:31.787 --> 01:23:33.662
Stand back! Coming forward!


01:23:33.746 --> 01:23:34.954
Diver's down there.


01:23:35.704 --> 01:23:37.224
Must've been something valuable.


01:23:37.287 --> 01:23:38.621
That's for the trawler.


01:23:39.246 --> 01:23:41.204
They found somethin' else down there.


01:23:45.537 --> 01:23:48.497
That's it! Good lad!


01:24:13.662 --> 01:24:16.162
I never said nothing. Did I?


01:24:17.454 --> 01:24:19.079
She'll not come back now.


01:24:19.162 --> 01:24:21.912
The fishes will have
had her by now, ain't they?


01:24:23.537 --> 01:24:24.704
Frank.


01:24:26.496 --> 01:24:29.079
You really shouldn't be here.


01:24:36.537 --> 01:24:39.996
Don't wait there. Come on.
Everybody move. Stand back.


01:24:48.329 --> 01:24:52.037
The body was found in her boat.
The same color hair.


01:24:52.662 --> 01:24:56.496
And the engravings on her wedding ring.
There's no doubt it's her.


01:24:56.579 --> 01:24:58.204
Don't be an imbecile.


01:24:59.079 --> 01:25:02.162
I'm sure there's a perfectly logical
explanation, hmm?


01:25:02.246 --> 01:25:03.746
You don't think it's odd?


01:25:03.829 --> 01:25:07.078
That your brother identified and buried
the body of a stranger as his wife?


01:25:07.161 --> 01:25:08.870
No, Giles, I don't.


01:25:09.536 --> 01:25:12.286
If you're so concerned,
go and ask Maxim yourself.


01:25:12.370 --> 01:25:15.329
I would, but no one's
seen him for hours. I mean...


01:25:17.037 --> 01:25:20.287
What's happened?
Why were the police questioning him?


01:25:23.079 --> 01:25:26.287
No. He's not been home.
Why? When did they release him?


01:25:27.537 --> 01:25:29.537
<i>...please, do let me know
when you see him.</i>


01:25:29.621 --> 01:25:33.370
Yes, of course, Frank. Thank you.


01:25:33.453 --> 01:25:35.536
<i>Don't worry. Take care of yourself.</i>


01:26:25.078 --> 01:26:27.161
It's over. She's won.


01:26:29.453 --> 01:26:30.536
Who's won?


01:26:32.828 --> 01:26:34.078
Rebecca.


01:26:38.495 --> 01:26:43.037
If that's her body they found,
who is it you buried?


01:26:44.495 --> 01:26:45.495
I don't know.


01:26:46.411 --> 01:26:47.578
Maxim.


01:26:49.745 --> 01:26:50.745
The truth.


01:26:52.120 --> 01:26:54.411
I don't know. I swear it.


01:26:57.078 --> 01:26:58.161
How did she drown?


01:26:59.620 --> 01:27:00.620
She didn't.


01:27:01.161 --> 01:27:02.453
Don't lie to me.


01:27:03.286 --> 01:27:04.703
She didn't drown.


01:27:06.078 --> 01:27:07.161
She was already dead.


01:27:08.619 --> 01:27:09.910
Her boat was damaged.


01:27:11.035 --> 01:27:12.245
I damaged it.


01:27:13.995 --> 01:27:15.161
Deliberately.


01:27:19.245 --> 01:27:20.245
Oh, Maxim.


01:27:21.370 --> 01:27:22.536
You didn't know her.


01:27:23.786 --> 01:27:25.036
Nobody did.


01:27:28.286 --> 01:27:30.453
She told me on our honeymoon
how it would be.


01:27:31.245 --> 01:27:33.119
How she would keep her flat in London.


01:27:33.952 --> 01:27:37.202
Her parade of men. Even her own cousin.


01:27:38.160 --> 01:27:39.160
Please, Maxim!


01:27:40.702 --> 01:27:43.745
She relished it. Playing the part.


01:27:44.453 --> 01:27:48.370
The perfect wife,
knowing that I would never divorce her.


01:27:48.453 --> 01:27:50.036
'Cause you loved her.


01:27:53.078 --> 01:27:55.536
I hated her.


01:27:58.285 --> 01:27:59.577
Hated her cruelty.


01:28:01.244 --> 01:28:02.994
I hated my cowardice.


01:28:04.619 --> 01:28:09.285
Knowing that I wouldn't divorce her.
Knowing I could never do that to our name.


01:28:16.911 --> 01:28:17.995
How did she die?


01:28:18.703 --> 01:28:20.078
When she came back from London,


01:28:20.161 --> 01:28:22.702
she told me
she was expecting a visit from Favell.


01:28:23.785 --> 01:28:25.660
When I got here, she was alone.


01:28:25.744 --> 01:28:27.452
She looked different. She was pale.


01:28:28.702 --> 01:28:30.660
She'd seen a doctor in London.


01:28:30.744 --> 01:28:36.285
She said, "Imagine if I had a child, Max.
You could never prove it wasn't yours."


01:28:36.369 --> 01:28:39.286
See, it wasn't enough
for her to take my pride.


01:28:40.703 --> 01:28:44.078
She wanted to take
my name, my home, everything.


01:28:44.828 --> 01:28:48.410
And she said, "Go on, Max, do it."


01:28:49.327 --> 01:28:52.285
"All you have to do is
pull the trigger and you'll be free."


01:28:54.619 --> 01:28:55.619
Please.


01:29:19.327 --> 01:29:21.035
Bullet went straight through her.


01:29:21.702 --> 01:29:24.452
She didn't fall right away.
She just stood there.


01:29:25.160 --> 01:29:26.452
So calm.


01:29:27.827 --> 01:29:29.160
Almost relieved.


01:29:32.494 --> 01:29:33.827
And then she was gone.


01:29:37.201 --> 01:29:39.994
All this time
I thought you still loved Rebecca.


01:30:04.909 --> 01:30:06.284
Why didn't you tell me?


01:30:14.285 --> 01:30:15.494
I couldn't.


01:30:18.369 --> 01:30:20.702
I was so afraid I'd have lost you.


01:30:23.952 --> 01:30:26.076
Go to the police, tell them everything.


01:30:26.951 --> 01:30:30.534
You didn't know. Nothing'll happen to you.


01:30:34.034 --> 01:30:36.827
I understand
if you want nothing more to do with me.


01:30:38.285 --> 01:30:39.410
That's your choice.


01:30:43.410 --> 01:30:48.244
You made a mistake...
identifying the body.


01:30:49.243 --> 01:30:51.243
It was the grief, the trauma.


01:30:53.034 --> 01:30:55.368
Nobody knows but us.
Nobody will ever know.


01:30:57.784 --> 01:30:59.326
No, she hasn't won, Maxim.


01:31:00.159 --> 01:31:01.243
She hasn't won.


01:31:02.159 --> 01:31:03.243
We won't let her.


01:31:25.201 --> 01:31:26.826
You don't have to speak to them.


01:31:26.909 --> 01:31:29.576
<i>All stand
for the Right Honorable James Crouch.</i>


01:31:33.743 --> 01:31:34.744
Stand back.


01:31:34.785 --> 01:31:37.369
<i>Order! Settle down.</i>


01:31:37.452 --> 01:31:39.701
<i>This is the... Sit down, sir.</i>


01:31:39.784 --> 01:31:42.118
<i>This is the coroner's inquest</i>


01:31:42.201 --> 01:31:45.243
<i>into the discovery
of the body of Rebecca de Winter.</i>


01:31:45.326 --> 01:31:48.493
<i>This is not
currently a criminal proceeding.</i>


01:31:48.576 --> 01:31:51.659
We are here
only to ascertain how Mrs. de Winter died.


01:31:52.493 --> 01:31:56.076
The court will now hear from
Detective Welch of the Kerrith police.


01:31:56.868 --> 01:31:57.868
Detective Welch.


01:31:59.868 --> 01:32:03.200
The body
Mr. de Winter identified last year...


01:32:04.326 --> 01:32:05.326
was not his wife.


01:32:06.243 --> 01:32:11.201
In fact, Rebecca de Winter's body
was recovered from the cabin of her boat.


01:32:11.993 --> 01:32:13.243
That troubled me.


01:32:13.326 --> 01:32:15.701
As did the nature
of the damage to the vessel.


01:32:15.784 --> 01:32:17.534
And what was that nature?


01:32:17.618 --> 01:32:19.909
We found four holes below the waterline


01:32:19.993 --> 01:32:22.534
consistent with those
made by a ship's gaff.


01:32:23.701 --> 01:32:25.576
- Or spike.
- Suggesting what?


01:32:25.659 --> 01:32:27.367
That the boat was deliberately scuttled.


01:32:29.033 --> 01:32:31.408
In my opinion, Mr. Coroner,


01:32:31.492 --> 01:32:34.284
this inquest can return
one of only two verdicts.


01:32:35.493 --> 01:32:38.784
Suicide or unlawful killing.


01:32:45.159 --> 01:32:47.534
<i>Your wife made a trip
to London the day she died.</i>


01:32:48.493 --> 01:32:49.493
It's time.


01:32:49.576 --> 01:32:53.075
In your statement to the police,
you say your wife seemed


01:32:53.158 --> 01:32:56.200
"preoccupied and unhappy"
when she returned.


01:32:56.908 --> 01:32:59.075
Don't be defensive.
Answer their questions calmly.


01:33:00.492 --> 01:33:02.493
What was the purpose
of her trip?


01:33:03.243 --> 01:33:04.284
No idea.


01:33:04.368 --> 01:33:05.993
Was it normal for your wife


01:33:06.076 --> 01:33:08.534
not to discuss such matters
with her husband?


01:33:08.618 --> 01:33:10.909
Are you implying
there were problems in my marriage?


01:33:11.493 --> 01:33:14.243
I'm trying to understand
how you apparently failed


01:33:14.326 --> 01:33:16.450
to recognize your own wife last year.


01:33:16.533 --> 01:33:19.367
She'd been two months at sea.
She drifted 20 miles.


01:33:19.450 --> 01:33:20.825
She was bloated, decomposing,


01:33:20.908 --> 01:33:23.575
her arms ripped off, `
and there was nothing left of her face.


01:33:24.700 --> 01:33:27.533
Order! Order!


01:33:32.534 --> 01:33:34.451
<i>I was arrogant and stupid.</i>


01:33:35.784 --> 01:33:38.618
- I lost my nerve.
- No, you were passionate.


01:33:39.243 --> 01:33:40.408
They'll believe it.


01:33:41.492 --> 01:33:43.825
Who else knows she saw a doctor in London?


01:33:47.158 --> 01:33:48.575
You, me, and the doctor.


01:33:49.700 --> 01:33:52.117
They're not likely
to find any physical evidence.


01:33:53.283 --> 01:33:54.783
Not after so long at sea.


01:33:57.242 --> 01:33:58.908
The doctor is all they have.


01:34:05.283 --> 01:34:08.575
I did tell Mr. Favell
he wasn't welcome, but he insisted.


01:34:09.367 --> 01:34:10.867
Thank you, Mrs. Danvers.


01:34:13.158 --> 01:34:14.867
What the hell do you want?


01:34:18.367 --> 01:34:20.408
Another whiskey and soda would be nice.


01:34:22.075 --> 01:34:23.283
It's about Rebecca,


01:34:23.367 --> 01:34:25.408
so you might want
to send your wife off to bed.


01:34:25.492 --> 01:34:28.325
I'm not going anywhere.
I know all about you and Rebecca.


01:34:29.033 --> 01:34:30.033
Oh, really?


01:34:31.033 --> 01:34:32.950
You know all about that, do you?


01:34:34.242 --> 01:34:36.075
You were close, Favell.


01:34:36.158 --> 01:34:38.075
If I'd caught you here
that night with her...


01:34:38.158 --> 01:34:39.450
He was never here that night.


01:34:39.533 --> 01:34:40.867
But she did invite me.


01:34:42.492 --> 01:34:43.742
And that's the point.


01:34:44.700 --> 01:34:48.742
Suicide or foul play,
that's what the chap said, wasn't it?


01:34:50.450 --> 01:34:52.908
Now, inviting someone over...


01:34:53.450 --> 01:34:55.907
doesn't really sound like
the sort of thing one would do


01:34:55.991 --> 01:34:58.616
if one was planning to end it all,
does it?


01:35:00.158 --> 01:35:03.450
And that's what's been
driving me mad this last year.


01:35:04.950 --> 01:35:06.950
But it's beginning to make sense.


01:35:08.450 --> 01:35:12.492
She finally decided to leave you.
Is that why you killed her?


01:35:13.908 --> 01:35:17.658
You've no proof.
It's your word against mine.


01:35:17.742 --> 01:35:18.741
No.


01:35:21.366 --> 01:35:23.449
It's your word against Rebecca's.


01:35:25.949 --> 01:35:28.075
"Come to Manders when you get this.


01:35:28.158 --> 01:35:29.992
I've something to tell you


01:35:30.075 --> 01:35:34.033
and I want to see you
as soon as possible. Rebecca."


01:35:35.325 --> 01:35:36.450
Let me see.


01:35:37.575 --> 01:35:39.718
- Get out of my house.
- Don't rise to it, Maxim.


01:35:39.742 --> 01:35:41.783
Yes. Don't rise to it, Max.


01:35:43.532 --> 01:35:45.657
I only came by to thank you, really.


01:35:46.532 --> 01:35:49.366
You've been so generous over the years,


01:35:49.449 --> 01:35:52.157
sharing your wife
with so many of us chaps.


01:35:53.491 --> 01:35:56.657
Actually, I wondered
if I might try my luck with the new one.


01:35:59.533 --> 01:36:01.783
There's that temper
I told you about.


01:36:02.783 --> 01:36:04.200
How much do you want?


01:36:06.617 --> 01:36:08.991
She's cleverer than she looks, this one,
isn't she?


01:36:11.074 --> 01:36:12.449
Seems to be a spot of blood.


01:36:13.491 --> 01:36:14.491
Oh, dearie me.


01:36:21.324 --> 01:36:22.574
She's right, though.


01:36:23.991 --> 01:36:25.574
I'm not a rich man, Max.


01:36:27.450 --> 01:36:29.158
Well, I'm too fond of gambling for that,


01:36:29.242 --> 01:36:33.366
but I do have a certain lifestyle
that I've come to enjoy.


01:36:35.991 --> 01:36:38.199
I imagine I could get by on around...


01:36:40.032 --> 01:36:42.491
£10,000 for the note


01:36:42.574 --> 01:36:45.657
and my silence
when I take the stand tomorrow.


01:36:45.741 --> 01:36:47.366
This is blackmail.


01:36:47.449 --> 01:36:49.824
- What are you doing?
- Calling the police.


01:36:49.907 --> 01:36:52.282
Yeah. Call the police.


01:36:54.699 --> 01:36:56.241
Might even put us in the same cell.


01:36:57.824 --> 01:36:58.907
Not for long, though.


01:36:59.699 --> 01:37:02.241
I imagine you're looking
at the noose, Maxim.


01:37:09.491 --> 01:37:11.699
At Inspector Welch's request,


01:37:11.782 --> 01:37:14.366
there's a change
to this morning's proceedings.


01:37:14.449 --> 01:37:16.032
We shall now hear


01:37:16.116 --> 01:37:19.366
from the de Winters' housekeeper,
Mrs. Danvers.


01:37:27.241 --> 01:37:29.199
Safe to say
not much occurs at Manderley


01:37:29.282 --> 01:37:31.866
without your knowledge
or say-so, would I be right?


01:37:31.949 --> 01:37:35.032
I ensure the smooth running of the house.


01:37:35.616 --> 01:37:37.324
Which is how
you came to be aware


01:37:37.407 --> 01:37:40.407
of the late Mrs. de Winter's
relationship with Mr. Favell.


01:37:41.282 --> 01:37:43.616
Well, I was
aware they were, um, intimate.


01:37:43.699 --> 01:37:45.781
But my lady's
private affairs were her own.


01:37:45.865 --> 01:37:47.156
So they should be.


01:37:47.240 --> 01:37:49.406
But since
these circumstances are far from normal,


01:37:49.490 --> 01:37:52.906
perhaps you'd share with the court
what you told me last night.


01:37:54.032 --> 01:37:56.616
I learned of a note
addressed to Mr. Favell.


01:37:57.407 --> 01:38:00.116
I urged him to share that note with you.


01:38:00.199 --> 01:38:04.241
A note Mr. de Winter
seemed keen to keep from this court.


01:38:04.324 --> 01:38:05.324
Yes.


01:38:06.116 --> 01:38:10.990
The note was inviting Mr. Favell
to join Mrs. de Winter at the house...


01:38:12.240 --> 01:38:13.906
the night my lady died.


01:38:14.573 --> 01:38:19.740
Mr. de Winter offered money
in exchange for that note.


01:38:19.823 --> 01:38:21.906
The note
was from Rebecca de Winter.


01:38:21.990 --> 01:38:22.990
It was.


01:38:23.657 --> 01:38:26.449
She wrote
she had urgent news to share with him.


01:38:27.282 --> 01:38:32.491
And how much was Mr. Favell offered?


01:38:33.074 --> 01:38:34.698
£10,000.


01:38:40.490 --> 01:38:41.490
A check...


01:38:42.948 --> 01:38:47.698
written by Mr. de Winter...
in exchange for the note.


01:38:47.781 --> 01:38:49.698
Where does it say that?
All you have is a check.


01:38:49.781 --> 01:38:52.302
- Nothing to say what it's for.
- Order! Madam, order.


01:38:53.324 --> 01:38:58.531
Mrs. Danvers, do you think it's likely
Rebecca de Winter drowned herself?


01:38:59.448 --> 01:39:01.031
No, sir. I do not.


01:39:01.115 --> 01:39:04.406
In the weeks, uh, leading up to her death,


01:39:04.490 --> 01:39:09.906
she had become
fatigued and was feeling sick.


01:39:11.031 --> 01:39:14.781
And she asked me
to let out the waistband in her trousers.


01:39:14.865 --> 01:39:17.531
Her belly was growing.


01:39:22.324 --> 01:39:24.990
Mrs. de Winter went to London
the day she died. Did she say why?


01:39:25.490 --> 01:39:26.656
- No.
- Odd.


01:39:26.740 --> 01:39:29.948
It must've been something deeply personal
for her to have kept that from me.


01:39:30.031 --> 01:39:32.531
Like, say, an appointment with her doctor.


01:39:32.615 --> 01:39:35.573
Not her family doctor,
as you might expect, but someone discreet.


01:39:37.240 --> 01:39:38.740
Away from prying eyes


01:39:38.823 --> 01:39:42.240
as if news of her condition
was something she wished to keep private.


01:39:42.323 --> 01:39:47.572
A wish to share
only with her lover, Jack Favell.


01:39:48.405 --> 01:39:52.240
- You murdering bastard.
- You're a murdering bastard!


01:39:52.323 --> 01:39:54.823
With my child! I hope they hang you.


01:39:54.906 --> 01:39:57.490
I hope they hang you!
You murdered Rebecca!


01:39:57.573 --> 01:39:59.073
Only two possible verdicts.


01:39:59.156 --> 01:40:02.948
I hope you agree, sir,
that there's no motive at all for suicide.


01:40:03.031 --> 01:40:05.823
But a clear one for murder.


01:40:05.906 --> 01:40:09.865
This inquest is suspended
pending a criminal investigation.


01:40:09.948 --> 01:40:12.405
Ladies and gentlemen, court is adjourned.


01:40:13.655 --> 01:40:15.155
Nobody's above the law.


01:40:16.405 --> 01:40:18.697
Get your hands off me! Get off!


01:40:18.780 --> 01:40:20.073
Mrs. Danvers.


01:40:20.656 --> 01:40:22.365
Say nothing. They can't prove anything.


01:40:22.448 --> 01:40:24.531
I want her appointment books,
diaries, address books,


01:40:24.615 --> 01:40:26.156
household finances, everything.


01:40:26.240 --> 01:40:29.281
She saw that doctor sometime
and she paid him.


01:40:30.323 --> 01:40:33.115
Roe, start placing calls
to women specialists in London.


01:41:03.864 --> 01:41:05.780
No. No.


01:41:12.655 --> 01:41:15.780
I'm sorry, do you have
permission to search this place?


01:41:34.947 --> 01:41:36.489
Mrs. de Winter?


01:41:36.572 --> 01:41:37.947
- Oh, Frank!
- What?


01:41:38.030 --> 01:41:40.030
I need her checks, her bank statements.


01:41:40.114 --> 01:41:42.447
Anything that has
the name and address of her doctor.


01:41:42.530 --> 01:41:45.239
Right. Here it is. I know what you need.


01:41:47.615 --> 01:41:49.822
- I need a doctor.
- You need her doctor? There.


01:41:52.239 --> 01:41:53.739
That must be it.


01:41:55.739 --> 01:41:56.859
Shame on you.


01:41:57.364 --> 01:41:59.864
Shame on you for taking his side.


01:41:59.947 --> 01:42:02.489
I'm not taking anyone's side,
Mrs. Danvers. I...


01:42:02.572 --> 01:42:07.155
And you, Frank.
Licking Mr. de Winter's boots by day,


01:42:07.239 --> 01:42:09.947
and pawing at the cottage door at night.


01:42:10.030 --> 01:42:12.197
Sobbing like a schoolboy.


01:42:13.364 --> 01:42:15.363
She despised you all.


01:42:16.446 --> 01:42:19.280
The men in London,
the men at the Manderley parties.


01:42:19.864 --> 01:42:22.489
You were nothing but playthings for her.


01:42:23.780 --> 01:42:27.072
And why shouldn't a woman amuse herself?


01:42:30.697 --> 01:42:34.947
She lived her life
as she pleased, my Rebecca.


01:42:38.530 --> 01:42:40.696
No wonder a man had to kill her.


01:42:43.238 --> 01:42:44.638
It must have hurt.


01:42:45.905 --> 01:42:49.822
Knowing your only friend in the world
took a secret like that to her grave.


01:42:53.364 --> 01:42:55.072
Pack your bags, Mrs. Danvers.


01:42:56.114 --> 01:42:57.947
I expect you gone by nightfall.


01:44:45.113 --> 01:44:48.154
- Miss?
- Terribly sorry, I've left my purse.


01:44:48.238 --> 01:44:49.988
Who was it you saw, Miss?


01:44:50.613 --> 01:44:51.904
Dr. John Baker.


01:44:58.404 --> 01:44:59.571
Thank you.


01:45:06.070 --> 01:45:07.112
Wait there.


01:45:16.779 --> 01:45:19.099
- Dr. Baker, sir.
- Good evening, Tas.


01:45:23.779 --> 01:45:24.863
"Danvers."


01:45:36.612 --> 01:45:39.403
I see so many patients.


01:45:42.279 --> 01:45:43.988
I can't remember her.


01:45:44.071 --> 01:45:46.904
Maybe it'll
come back when you see her file.


01:45:51.446 --> 01:45:54.612
It would have been more
convenient to read the file to begin with.


01:45:57.653 --> 01:45:59.695
We'll do what we can to help.


01:45:59.778 --> 01:46:02.445
Oh, no. This is not as it should be.


01:46:04.403 --> 01:46:05.653
Where's she gone now?


01:46:06.237 --> 01:46:07.237
Who?


01:46:08.820 --> 01:46:10.363
The young woman who was here.


01:46:13.571 --> 01:46:14.904
It's not here.


01:46:15.529 --> 01:46:17.279
I'll have a word with my secretary.


01:46:20.945 --> 01:46:23.112
It's possible
she misplaced it.


01:46:23.695 --> 01:46:27.945
This girl. Is there any way
she could get out of here?


01:46:58.695 --> 01:47:01.653
I read it, that's all.
I haven't changed a word Dr. Baker wrote.


01:47:01.737 --> 01:47:05.653
Rebecca Danvers.
Yes, now I remember. Terrible thing.


01:47:05.737 --> 01:47:08.570
That wasn't her real name.
And she wasn't pregnant.


01:47:08.653 --> 01:47:10.445
Then why would she use a false name?


01:47:10.528 --> 01:47:12.903
Why would she come all the way to London


01:47:12.987 --> 01:47:15.320
to make an appointment with you
and not her family doctor?


01:47:15.403 --> 01:47:18.445
Perhaps she wanted
to spare her family the news.


01:47:18.528 --> 01:47:20.195
That the baby wasn't her husband's?


01:47:20.278 --> 01:47:24.278
Inspector, I am not
that kind of women's specialist.


01:47:24.362 --> 01:47:28.612
I'm not an obstetrician.
My field is oncology.


01:47:28.695 --> 01:47:32.070
I treat cancers
of the reproductive system.


01:47:32.153 --> 01:47:34.652
The bloating, the fatigue.
They're common symptoms.


01:47:36.319 --> 01:47:37.569
She had cancer.


01:47:39.903 --> 01:47:41.570
There's her news for Jack Favell.


01:47:41.653 --> 01:47:44.028
That doesn't prove she killed herself.


01:47:44.112 --> 01:47:46.403
She wouldn't have wanted to suffer.


01:47:46.487 --> 01:47:48.612
Yes, she told me as much.


01:47:49.362 --> 01:47:51.987
She was very advanced
by the time she was symptomatic.


01:47:52.070 --> 01:47:53.487
Saw her first in April,


01:47:53.570 --> 01:47:56.820
by May, it was clear
she was too far gone for treatment.


01:47:56.903 --> 01:48:00.736
She only had weeks
and the pain would have been considerable.


01:48:02.111 --> 01:48:03.236
How did she do it?


01:48:05.819 --> 01:48:08.153
She took out her boat and scuttled it.


01:48:09.528 --> 01:48:10.862
She drowned herself.


01:48:53.694 --> 01:48:55.361
Stroke of luck for you there, Max.


01:49:05.027 --> 01:49:06.612
I bet you think you've won, don't you?


01:49:08.403 --> 01:49:11.361
Well, maybe the law can't get you.
I still can.


01:49:13.194 --> 01:49:15.152
Is there anything else you want to say?


01:49:16.319 --> 01:49:17.719
If there is, you better say it now.


01:49:31.902 --> 01:49:34.111
Do you know what I hate her for most?


01:49:35.694 --> 01:49:37.527
It's what she's taken from you.


01:49:38.569 --> 01:49:42.986
It's gone forever. That funny, young,
lost look I loved so much.


01:49:44.694 --> 01:49:46.527
You're not that person anymore.


01:49:47.152 --> 01:49:48.694
Don't hate her for that.


01:50:33.152 --> 01:50:36.194
What's that burning?
Oh, my God, that's Manderley.


01:50:44.777 --> 01:50:46.361
Come on! Get away from there.


01:50:46.444 --> 01:50:49.276
Get off the lawn! Go! Come on!


01:50:51.026 --> 01:50:52.986
Get off the lawn!
Frith, get off the lawn!


01:50:53.068 --> 01:50:54.860
How many people are inside?
Is everyone out?


01:50:54.943 --> 01:50:58.318
- I don't know, sir.
- You all right? What happened, Clarice?


01:50:58.401 --> 01:50:59.485
I saw her.


01:50:59.568 --> 01:51:01.568
What do you mean?
Who did you see?


01:51:01.610 --> 01:51:03.027
Mrs. Danvers.


01:51:03.111 --> 01:51:06.236
Help her! Where are the hoses?


01:51:06.319 --> 01:51:10.527
- Where is she?
- She went to the boat house.


01:52:19.193 --> 01:52:21.360
Mrs. Danvers! Please!


01:52:22.818 --> 01:52:23.985
Please come away.


01:52:25.276 --> 01:52:27.275
You asked for my help. Here it is.


01:52:28.025 --> 01:52:29.735
Mrs. Danvers, please.


01:52:30.735 --> 01:52:33.068
He killed the only person I loved.


01:52:34.651 --> 01:52:36.235
I can't let you have Manderley.


01:52:37.568 --> 01:52:39.110
It was ours, you see.


01:52:40.985 --> 01:52:42.443
You don't have to do this.


01:52:42.526 --> 01:52:46.985
I know you'll stand by him.
But you'll never know happiness.


01:52:50.485 --> 01:52:51.525
Yes, I will.


01:53:53.275 --> 01:53:55.984
<i>Last night,
I dreamt I went to Manderley again.</i>


01:53:58.693 --> 01:54:01.443
<i>I dreamt of Mrs. Danvers and of Rebecca.</i>


01:54:06.067 --> 01:54:10.650
<i>But this morning I woke up
and left the dead behind.</i>


01:54:13.067 --> 01:54:17.192
<i>And as I sit before the mirror
in our stuffy little room in Cairo,</i>


01:54:18.734 --> 01:54:22.234
<i>just another stop
on our quest to find a real home,</i>


01:54:24.400 --> 01:54:26.317
<i>I can see the woman I am now.</i>


01:54:28.651 --> 01:54:31.484
<i>And I know
that I have made the right decision...</i>


01:54:34.650 --> 01:54:37.859
<i>to save the one thing
worth walking through flames for.</i>


01:54:40.942 --> 01:54:41.942
<i>Love.</i>

